100%.

119
00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:30.610
Out of the womb basically.

120
00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.120
I mean like the animal thing for you was from the get-go.

121
00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.795
Right?
It really was.

122
00:04:34.795 --> 00:04:37.653
So there's something I have this theory.

123
00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.710
I remember talking to Gene Baur about this.

124
00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.670
Like I just think that Gene,

125
00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.510
like people like Gene come out different,

126
00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:47.180
and they're like super sensitive,

127
00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:48.930
to the way the world operates.
I agree.

128
00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:52.590
And it leads them down this certain path,

129
00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.680
but not everyone's wired that way.

130
00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.040
'Cause like I came at, you know,

131
00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.740
I've been vegan plant-based for 14 years now,

132
00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:01.410
but animal rights, wasn't my entry point.

133
00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.150
Like that's become really important to me

134
00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.690
but that wasn't initially.
It was health.

135
00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:05.763
Yeah, it was more of a health thing.

136
00:05:05.763 --> 00:05:07.630
And it was like a vanity thing.

137
00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:10.620
If I'm being honest, there was a selfishness to it,

138
00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:14.880
that now, you know, I've become much more attuned,

139
00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.640
and sensitive, and passionate, about the other things

140
00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:19.600
but I'm not wired that way.

141
00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:24.370
The way like you are, or Gene, or Shaun, or Joaquin,

142
00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:25.330
or these other people,

143
00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.810
that just carry that sensitivity

144
00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:30.500
which probably makes their life experience very painful.

145
00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:35.500
It is well, an empath's path is it is really painful.

146
00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:37.563
I mean, you nailed it.

147
00:05:37.563 --> 00:05:38.396
That's exactly it,

148
00:05:38.396 --> 00:05:41.870
cause you're sort of like you can't shut off that feeling.

149
00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:43.790
And I remember like being a kid

150
00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:48.790
and sort of witnessing just cruelty in general,

151
00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:53.400
whether it was to another adult, or a child, or an animal.

152
00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:57.880
And I remember feeling a lot of pain over that,

153
00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.320
and it didn't have to be my own pain.

154
00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:03.640
I hated seeing people in pain, a life in pain.

155
00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:04.607
Let's put it that way,

156
00:06:04.607 --> 00:06:06.500
because the animals included obviously were a big thing.

157
00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:09.880
But I did witness a lot of that cruelty as a kid.

158
00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:12.920
And I remember when it came through the animals,

159
00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:17.450
it was especially unfair because they had no choice.

160
00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:18.510
They couldn't get away.

161
00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:19.390
They couldn't call for help.

162
00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:20.900
There's no nine one one, you know

163
00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:24.050
for a dog that's getting beaten up, or tied outside,

164
00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:27.260
or you know, hurt in any way, or a cat, or whatever it is.

165
00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:31.210
Like they don't have the resource, you know, to do that.

166
00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:33.800
And so it does take us.

167
00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.670
It does take an outside source to say,

168
00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:36.865
I don't think that's right.

169
00:06:36.865 --> 00:06:37.993
That doesn't seem right to me.

170
00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:41.805
So Earthlings was like 2005, right?

171
00:06:41.805 --> 00:06:42.638
Yeah.

172
00:06:42.638 --> 00:06:45.620
So you couldn't have been, back from Hong Kong

173
00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:47.500
very long before that took place.

174
00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.100
Like how did that come together?

175
00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.550
You know, Shaun pioneered, obviously everything,

176
00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:54.610
Shaun was already on it, collecting footage,

177
00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:56.410
doing everything he was doing.

178
00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:59.060
And you know, when I got back, when I moved back

179
00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:03.470
from Asia to the States, it was like,

180
00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:06.530
I was changed by actually by PETA,

181
00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:08.180
you know, PETA was the group,

182
00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:09.810
and as you know PETA is not a shy group, (laughs).

183
00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:12.760
Yeah, not quite.
No, not quite

184
00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:14.580
I wouldn't use that word.

185
00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.773
But PETA as it were, was opening,

186
00:07:18.991 --> 00:07:21.810
an Asian office at the time.

187
00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:24.300
And so I didn't even know they had a presence in Asia.

188
00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.070
I mean, PETA, they're very famous.

189
00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:28.520
So you know about what they do at New York fashion week,

190
00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:29.410
and all this sort of stuff.

191
00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:31.170
And it's all very sensationalized,

192
00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:33.750
and kind of like, you know, this sort of fun thing,

193
00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:35.290
cultural thing that people make fun of.

194
00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:36.730
But in Asia,

195
00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:39.240
there really was no representation for the animals.

196
00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:40.910
I mean, at that time it was sort of like,

197
00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:43.770
animals Asia, who's still in business.

198
00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:45.210
And there have been around for about 30 years,

199
00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:46.510
but other than them,

200
00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:48.090
like these bigger more organized groups,

201
00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:49.320
like hadn't come in.

202
00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.740
So they come in to open this office

203
00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:51.650
and that's what changed me.

204
00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:53.810
So I was already changed when I was living in Asia

205
00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:56.790
because I was sort of like this self-professed animal lover,

206
00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.862
but was still doing all the things

207
00:07:58.862 --> 00:08:02.450
that were cruel and unacceptable.

208
00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:05.900
And so that's why, as we were talking earlier

209
00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:07.360
it's very easy to like meet people,

210
00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.500
where they are and have compassion.

211
00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.960
People don't get it, because I was that person.

212
00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.380
I can't, you know what I mean?

213
00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:15.180
I wasn't born conscious, I was born empathic.

214
00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:16.610
I was born sensitive.

215
00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:19.130
But I wasn't born like understanding it

216
00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:20.970
from a larger perspective

217
00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:24.160
and going, oh, okay, well, my action has a chain reaction

218
00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:27.770
and this is what's happening in that chain.

219
00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:28.920
So I was changed already.

220
00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:31.930
And then when I came over, and met Shaun,

221
00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:33.593
it was just like that perfect timing,

222
00:08:33.593 --> 00:08:36.570
of like, I was just new, and kind of ripe in this.

223
00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.627
I'd come from a region where animal rights, and cruelty,

224
00:08:39.627 --> 00:08:42.290
and the voice of animals is non-existent.

225
00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:45.678
And so I was really on fire, to like get this message out.

226
00:08:45.678 --> 00:08:49.041
And I think that the easiest, if you can call it that,

227
00:08:49.041 --> 00:08:52.600
region in the world to do that, is the West.

228
00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:53.810
If you're gonna start with anywhere.

229
00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:56.490
Yeah, I can't imagine the temperature in Asia,

230
00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:59.850
around animal rights is anything remotely similar

231
00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:00.683
to what it is here.

232
00:09:00.683 --> 00:09:01.516
Not even.

233
00:09:01.516 --> 00:09:04.340
I mean the spotlight, the discussion,

234
00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:06.272
I mean they're still coming to it,

235
00:09:06.272 --> 00:09:10.330
and we're getting there because of this younger generation.

236
00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:11.500
I mean I think we're getting there,

237
00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:12.970
because of what we were talking about earlier,

238
00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:14.710
about kids changing their parents.

239
00:09:14.710 --> 00:09:17.220
And kids having a different kind of compassion

240
00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.904
than their parents did.

241
00:09:18.904 --> 00:09:22.180
But, you know, I'm the daughter of an immigrant mother,

242
00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:24.950
my mother, like, fled from a war-torn country,

243
00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:25.930
and came to the United States,

244
00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:28.880
and like, her emo was not like,

245
00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:32.819
oh, how are the dogs feeling? (laughs)

246
00:09:32.819 --> 00:09:34.809
You know, I haven't gotten here to save some cats

247
00:09:34.809 --> 00:09:38.490
Let me hear what my daughter has to say about the world.

248
00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:40.090
Exactly.

249
00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:41.170
I remember once complaining,

250
00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:43.530
about like the toothpaste or something.

251
00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:45.010
It was too mint or too strong.

252
00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:46.300
It was like some cheap toothpaste.

253
00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:48.330
And obviously everything we bought was on sale

254
00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.580
and I didn't grow up with money,

255
00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:50.820
and I complained about the toothpaste

256
00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:53.080
and she was just like, oh really?

257
00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:53.920
Oh really?

258
00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:55.300
The toothpaste that we can afford

259
00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:56.780
is not good enough for you.

