00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:58.150
And that toothpaste went away fast.

261
00:09:58.150 --> 00:09:58.983
She was like, you know what?

262
00:09:58.983 --> 00:10:00.734
You can get a job, buy your own toothpaste.

263
00:10:00.734 --> 00:10:02.365
(Rich and Maggie laugh)

264
00:10:02.365 --> 00:10:04.560
So your mom's Vietnamese,

265
00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:07.280
and your dad was deployed to Vietnam.

266
00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:08.971
That's right, yeah, they met in the way.

267
00:10:08.971 --> 00:10:10.063
So they met there, wow.

268
00:10:10.063 --> 00:10:11.550
But you were born in Hawaii?

269
00:10:11.550 --> 00:10:12.383
I was born in Hawaii.

270
00:10:12.383 --> 00:10:13.760
I have a brother and sister who were born there,

271
00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:15.810
and then they were married,

272
00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:18.780
they came here, and then they had three more kids,

273
00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:20.570
of which I'm the youngest of five.

274
00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:21.660
Right.
Yeah.

275
00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:23.430
So grew up in Oahu?

276
00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:24.410
Born and raised, yep.

277
00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:25.410
Yeah.

278
00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:26.860
Oahu girl.
Oahu girl, yeah.

279
00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:28.120
How was that like?

280
00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:29.770
Well, you know, I mean, it's...

281
00:10:31.598 --> 00:10:34.670
You're connection to nature is,

282
00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:37.060
and your upbringing is sort of one in the same, right?

283
00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:39.140
So there's no separation between you,

284
00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:43.227
and like respect for all that we have in Hawaiian,

285
00:10:43.227 --> 00:10:44.140
and you lived in Hawaii.

286
00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:45.340
So you understand this, right?

287
00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:48.670
It's sort of like, we don't litter, we don't do this.

288
00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:49.503
We don't do that.

289
00:10:49.503 --> 00:10:50.527
I mean, we don't harm the environment.

290
00:10:50.527 --> 00:10:51.360
And we're trying.

291
00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.658
I mean, there are people,

292
00:10:52.658 --> 00:10:54.980
there are always people who do what they do.

293
00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:59.980
But we really do sort of live this profound connection

294
00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:01.810
to the world around us.

295
00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:04.300
And that's a very Island mentality.

296
00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:07.360
And so I think that's what gave me

297
00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:10.380
my connection to the oceans in a very real way.

298
00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:14.430
It was like, I remember just having this respect

299
00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.610
for the ocean that was so different

300
00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:17.810
than people that I'd met,

301
00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:19.510
you know who grew up on the mainland and what not.

302
00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:21.898
Because that was a world that was undiscovered,

303
00:11:21.898 --> 00:11:25.270
we really know very little about, to be honest.

304
00:11:25.270 --> 00:11:26.570
I mean, we thing we know a lot,

305
00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:28.732
and we know nothing about the ocean.

306
00:11:28.732 --> 00:11:33.460
And yet, somehow we feel that the ocean is at our disposal.

307
00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.265
And I remember as a kid thinking, no, no,

308
00:11:35.265 --> 00:11:40.265
the respect that I had for it was almost like a fear

309
00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.260
that you have for someone you respect, you know,

310
00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.093
like a superior.

311
00:11:43.093 --> 00:11:45.200
I kinda felt like the ocean was my superior.

312
00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.830
And I had this like, you know, this respect

313
00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:50.540
that came from a place of like almost fear,

314
00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.660
because it's such an unknown.

315
00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:55.140
And yet it provides so much for us.

316
00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:57.830
We take, and we don't know much.

317
00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:00.310
There is a weird energy in Hawaii.

318
00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:01.438
Like you can feel it.

319
00:12:01.438 --> 00:12:02.517
There's a darkness.
Oh yeah.

320
00:12:02.517 --> 00:12:03.430
And there's a lightness.

321
00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:04.263
There's a heaviness.

322
00:12:04.263 --> 00:12:07.460
Like I find myself, I was there in January for a month

323
00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.990
on the big Island and-

324
00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:11.285
Oh, I was there the whole of December, funny.

325
00:12:11.285 --> 00:12:12.200
Oh were you?
Yeah.

326
00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:13.230
On the big Island?

327
00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:14.813
Oh you were cool.
Yeah.

328
00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:19.020
You definitely have this...

329
00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:20.230
there's a sense of reverence,

330
00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:23.530
but also like, like, oh, like I'm very conscious

331
00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:26.827
of making sure that I put away my garbage in the right way-

332
00:12:26.827 --> 00:12:27.660
100%

333
00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:29.110
That I don't like move any of the rocks.

334
00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:31.897
And it's like, I don't wanna like upset (indistinct).

335
00:12:31.897 --> 00:12:34.513
Yeah, exactly, (laughs)
There's that whiplash.

336
00:12:34.513 --> 00:12:36.790
You don't want her to brake.
Yeah on the island,

337
00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:38.660
and I noticed that living in Kauai was...

338
00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:40.750
I had Laird Hamilton here not too long ago,

339
00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:41.830
and we were talking about that.

340
00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:44.665
Like, you can feel,

341
00:12:44.665 --> 00:12:47.910
there's like karma comes faster in Hawaii,

342
00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:49.737
I feel like, you know-
That's funny.

343
00:12:49.737 --> 00:12:50.820
There's a checks and balance.
I don't know what that is,

344
00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:53.210
but there's a sensibility around that.

345
00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:56.030
Well, It's a deeply spiritual place,

346
00:12:56.030 --> 00:12:59.030
you know, number one, and in any time you have a connection

347
00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:02.040
or a closeness to native culture, you're gonna feel that.

348
00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:04.210
I mean, I even feel it like when I'm on native land,

349
00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:06.330
like in Arizona, or in different places in the US.

350
00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:11.300
Like there's just a different spiritual penetration

351
00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:14.640
and awareness in everything you do.

352
00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:17.260
And so there's a checks an balance is different.

353
00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:19.900
It's almost like if you felt that angels, or guides

354
00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:21.260
or something were closer to you,

355
00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:23.160
and you if you felt that they were watching you.

356
00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:25.060
Yeah, there is that sense of being watched-

357
00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:25.893
Yes absolutely.

358
00:13:25.893 --> 00:13:28.800
And there's also-
It's ancestral it really is.

359
00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:31.460
Me being like a white dude, like, it's very different,

360
00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:32.630
I've spent enough time in Hawaii.

361
00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:35.140
Like I know what it's like to be in Hawaii,

362
00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:36.830
not at the resort, you know?

363
00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:40.207
Like to be in where people-
Real people live.

364
00:13:40.207 --> 00:13:41.850
Have been living for generations,

365
00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:43.947
like native inhabitants and stuff like that.

366
00:13:43.947 --> 00:13:46.130
And so there's also, you know

367
00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:49.560
a palpable sense of like, you're a visitor here.

368
00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:51.360
Like this is not your place.

369
00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:55.030
Oh we make people feel like that though, (laughs).

370
00:13:55.030 --> 00:13:56.333
Yes, for sure, right?

371
00:13:56.333 --> 00:13:59.250
Like, you better tread lightly dude.

372
00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:00.570
Or you're gonna get into trouble,

373
00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:03.130
and it's gonna go South quick on you.

374
00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:04.700
Yeah, I mean Hawaii is the only one I know of

375
00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:06.320
where like white is not my...

376
00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:08.450
you know, I mean the rest of the United States,

377
00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:10.520
and I mean, the first time I experienced

378
00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:14.890
somebody that was like, kinda treated me differently

379
00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:16.200
was like when I lived in Japan,

380
00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:17.940
and it was like a bunch of white girls from Texas,

381
00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:20.060
and they thought I was Mexican.

382
00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:23.110
At which, if I was what's the problem with that.

383
00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:24.790
And so they started, they wouldn't talk to me,

384
00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:26.880
and it was this very strange thing of like,

385
00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:27.993
I just never experienced that.

386
00:14:27.993 --> 00:14:29.490
Because in Hawaii as you know,

387
00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:31.440
I mean everyone's mixed race and there's really no...

388
00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:35.480
And if you're white, you have to tread lightly.

389
00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:37.530
And if you're not, you know, it's a different existence.

390
00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:38.650
On Kauai is different,

391
00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:41.000
because it's so cosmopolitan comparatively

392
00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.061
to the rest of the islands.
It is a bigger city.

393
00:14:42.061 --> 00:14:43.990
And it's very much like a Japanese culture.

394
00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:46.250
100% it is, yeah.

