418
00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:48.660
You have a very, like unique, and interesting path.

419
00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:52.680
Like at 17, you end up going to Tokyo to model, right?

420
00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:53.963
Funnily enough, that you say that

421
00:15:53.963 --> 00:15:55.890
because when people ask me about that, I go,

422
00:15:55.890 --> 00:16:00.030
you know, it wasn't really that much different culturally

423
00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:01.413
from growing up in Hawaii, like all my...

424
00:16:01.413 --> 00:16:04.570
I would say 95% of my teachers growing up were Japanese.

425
00:16:04.570 --> 00:16:06.800
You know, so I'm just used to that sensibility,

426
00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:07.800
the food, the whole thing.

427
00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:10.817
But, obviously I was in a huge city, fast,

428
00:16:10.817 --> 00:16:13.628
expensive city, that was very foreign to me.

429
00:16:13.628 --> 00:16:15.630
How did that happen?

430
00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:17.150
Well, I was just a broke student.

431
00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:18.400
I mean, I was an athlete,

432
00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:23.070
my season was cross-country,

433
00:16:23.070 --> 00:16:25.220
and then swimming, and then track and field,

434
00:16:25.220 --> 00:16:28.020
and then, water polo here and there.

435
00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:29.640
And so that was my year.

436
00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:32.370
And I ended up sort of like, we were all swimmers

437
00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:34.790
my sisters and I, and one of them was a diver.

438
00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:37.310
But I think that it was decided for us,

439
00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:40.233
and then as I became an athlete and really got into it,

440
00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:44.817
my body and my skill dictated that I was actually a runner,

441
00:16:44.817 --> 00:16:46.800
and that really was what I excelled at.

442
00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:49.520
And then, it was distance running

443
00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:51.070
and started to get honed in, and honed in.

444
00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:54.080
And so that's where I got my scholarship from,

445
00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:54.913
was cross country.

446
00:16:54.913 --> 00:16:58.010
And I just, I couldn't do it.

447
00:16:58.010 --> 00:16:59.580
I was already living on my own.

448
00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:00.500
I was paying rent.

449
00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:01.790
I was working retail.

450
00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:03.950
I was trying to keep a scholarship

451
00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:06.990
to a private Catholic university that was-

452
00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:08.640
On Oahu?
On Oahu.

453
00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:11.550
That was expensive, and it wasn't a full scholarship.

454
00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:14.520
It was, 70%, something like that.

455
00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:16.500
So there was just really no way,

456
00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:17.800
I was gonna make those ends meet.

457
00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.740
Because, as you know as a college athlete,

458
00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:21.050
you're training in the morning before school,

459
00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:22.959
you're training after school.

460
00:17:22.959 --> 00:17:24.383
And then I had to have a job, and all the rest of it.

461
00:17:24.383 --> 00:17:27.311
And it was completely unsustainable.

462
00:17:27.311 --> 00:17:30.830
And at the I guess if you had like that support,

463
00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:32.940
or whatever it was and you didn't have to work,

464
00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:33.773
you could make it work,

465
00:17:33.773 --> 00:17:35.190
but I wasn't in that position.

466
00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:36.023
Yeah.
Yeah.

467
00:17:36.023 --> 00:17:36.870
So that's kinda how it happened.

468
00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:39.580
I had a girlfriend, beautiful friend, who said,

469
00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.620
you know I go to Tokyo in the summers,

470
00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:43.070
and I make a bunch of money and come back,

471
00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:44.950
and I'm like, wow, that sounds amazing (laughs).

472
00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:46.153
Yeah, right.

473
00:17:46.153 --> 00:17:48.063
But she was a legitimate model.

474
00:17:48.063 --> 00:17:49.980
So yeah, of course you go to Tokyo,

475
00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:52.190
and make money because you have a career,

476
00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:55.540
and experience, and you're an actual model.

477
00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:57.470
But she was such a good friend,

478
00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:58.460
and we're still friends today.

479
00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:00.850
And she felt really sorry for me.

480
00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:02.350
I think she was just sort of like,

481
00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:04.610
I dunno how this chick is gonna make it.

482
00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:07.840
I don't know how she's gonna sustain this lifestyle.

483
00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:12.840
And she got me a contract to go with her and I went with her

484
00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:16.330
and it was modeling in the nineties.

485
00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:17.820
It was indentured servitude.

486
00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.790
Yeah, I've heard stories,

487
00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:21.670
terrible stories about how-

488
00:18:21.670 --> 00:18:22.503
Oh awful.
Yeah,

489
00:18:22.503 --> 00:18:25.100
the indentured aspect of it is not good.

490
00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:27.620
Like most of the money is going towards...

491
00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:28.680
They're overcharging for all these things,

492
00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:30.590
and all the money that you make.

493
00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:33.010
Yeah, they charge you like $5,000 US,

494
00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:35.090
in the nineties for one room.

495
00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:36.690
In an apartment where there's three other rooms

496
00:18:36.690 --> 00:18:39.701
and you're like, this seems like a lot, (laughs).

497
00:18:39.701 --> 00:18:41.170
Yeah, is it still that way?

498
00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:42.220
That sounds horrible.

499
00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:44.410
I think it is still that way on some level,

500
00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:46.520
especially like overseas, but it's just sort of like

501
00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:49.810
even just the mental aspect of like we have this agency,

502
00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:51.570
that was just awful, and you'd walk in,

503
00:18:51.570 --> 00:18:53.780
and there was a whiteboard right next to the door,

504
00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:55.700
where they weighed you every Friday.

505
00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:57.330
And they would put your names up,

506
00:18:57.330 --> 00:18:58.780
and like you had all the categories,

507
00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.870
and so you could walk and you could see everyone's weight.

508
00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.650
So if somebody was gaining weight,

509
00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:05.110
you know immediately you go,

510
00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:06.680
someone's a few pounds heavier.

511
00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:09.667
But that's what it was intended to shame you, you know?

512
00:19:09.667 --> 00:19:11.930
And the only reason that I was like the benchmark,

513
00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:13.330
they were like, oh, Maggie.

514
00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:15.300
Everyone's gonna be like Maggie, cause she stays skinny.

515
00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:18.590
I'm like, that's cause I can't afford it, (laughs).

516
00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:19.423
That's crazy.

517
00:19:19.423 --> 00:19:21.040
So you're working and booking stuff,

518
00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:22.670
and you still can't feed yourself?

519
00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:25.360
I wasn't booking stuff, 'cause I wasn't...

520
00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:27.680
I sort of booked like one commercial

521
00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:30.020
at the end of my long stay there, and it was a big one.

522
00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.800
And that's how I paid them back.

523
00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:35.140
But if I didn't get that, I wouldn't have been able to leave

524
00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:37.300
because I wouldn't have been paid back yet.

525
00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:41.000
So your friend who, you know, so kindly introduces you

526
00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:43.150
to this world, didn't tell you this part of it.

527
00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:46.188
She did, well she also had the dark underbelly,

528
00:19:46.188 --> 00:19:47.570
but she also-
You can come to Tokyo,

529
00:19:47.570 --> 00:19:51.462
but we're gonna live in a basement, you know eat-

530
00:19:51.462 --> 00:19:54.110
(indistinct) yeah, pretty much.

531
00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:57.300
But she has always lived that sort of charmed life.

532
00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:00.430
So she, I think her experience was, she always worked

533
00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:02.790
and always kind of like was able to pay the bills,

534
00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:05.410
and she was popular and very beautiful and people loved her.

535
00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:09.627
And so, you know, I think her view on it was her experience.

536
00:20:09.627 --> 00:20:11.523
And so it was quite good.

537
00:20:11.523 --> 00:20:12.356
(Maggie laughs)

538
00:20:12.356 --> 00:20:14.030
And did you, was this like a summer thing,

539
00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:15.492
or did you stop out of college to do it?

540
00:20:15.492 --> 00:20:16.325
It was like a summer thing, yeah.

541
00:20:16.325 --> 00:20:19.220
And then it sort of like bled into the fall a little bit.

542
00:20:19.220 --> 00:20:21.480
I went back to start school,

543
00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:24.930
and I had made enough money to like pay them back as I said,

544
00:20:24.930 --> 00:20:26.880
but I didn't make enough money to like,

545
00:20:28.502 --> 00:20:30.940
make my ends meet back where I was.

546
00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:35.940
And so she says, well, you know, next step Taipei.

547
00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:37.600
And I'm like, what?

548
00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:39.220
No, I hate traveling.

549
00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:40.210
I hate being in these places,

550
00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:41.770
where I don't speak the language, and I don't know anyone,

551
00:20:41.770 --> 00:20:44.400
this is so impossible.

552
00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:48.450
And she's like, no, no, Maggie, they'll like you they're.

553
00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:52.350
Won't be like Tokyo where they didn't like you, (laughs)

554
00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:54.100
Cause in Tokyo what they wanted,

555
00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:55.730
the blonde hair, blue eye girl-

556
00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:57.280
Well no what happened in the summer,

557
00:20:57.280 --> 00:21:00.810
is that there's was influx of like Eastern European,

558
00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:03.600
like Russian, like every girl and their mother.

559
00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:06.290
I mean that literally they bring their mothers.

560
00:21:06.290 --> 00:21:08.340
Comes to Tokyo, and there's like this influx

561
00:21:08.340 --> 00:21:10.070
of like four to 5,000 girls,

562
00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:10.990
that will come during the summer.

563
00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:13.473
So there's just a lot, it's very competitive.

564
00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.740
But we were a handful of mixed girls.

565
00:21:16.740 --> 00:21:20.030
So if they wanted mixed race girls, they knew where we were.

566
00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:22.860
But the rest were like, you know, pretty white guys.

567
00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:25.730
So a lot of competition, and that was the big deal.

568
00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:27.880
So I went to Taiwan, and when I got to Taiwan,

569
00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:30.680
that was actually when this trend of like blonde hair

570
00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:31.960
and blue eyes, that's all they wanted.

571
00:21:31.960 --> 00:21:34.170
So I'd walk into a room and they were like, get out.

572
00:21:34.170 --> 00:21:36.100
Like we don't even want to see you.

573
00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:38.300
So it was like are you either famous, and Chinese,

574
00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:39.648
or you were blonde with blue eyes.

575
00:21:39.648 --> 00:21:44.190
And so that rejection and that part of my life

576
00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.660
where I went there and nobody wants to see me

577
00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:47.833
and I didn't work,

578
00:21:48.690 --> 00:21:53.170
became a very lucky actually strike for me,

579
00:21:53.170 --> 00:21:55.490
because it pushed me to Hong Kong.

580
00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:56.323
Right.

581
00:21:56.323 --> 00:21:57.663
So how long were you in Taipei for then?

582
00:21:57.663 --> 00:21:59.680
I was probably there for like a few months.

583
00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:02.010
And it was just bad.

584
00:22:02.010 --> 00:22:03.490
It was just sad.

585
00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:06.323
And then, speak Cantonese?

586
00:22:06.323 --> 00:22:08.620
In Taipei was Mandarin.
Mandarin-

587
00:22:08.620 --> 00:22:10.180
So, I'm not Chinese,

588
00:22:10.180 --> 00:22:11.300
so I didn't speak a word.

589
00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:12.330
I had no clue what was going on.

590
00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:13.163
No friends.

591
00:22:13.163 --> 00:22:15.716
I had no, I mean, I was so lost (laughs).

592
00:22:15.716 --> 00:22:16.549
Right.

593
00:22:16.549 --> 00:22:18.053
So this is not going well,
This is not going well.

594
00:22:18.053 --> 00:22:19.590
You're going straight too
(Maggie laughs)

595
00:22:19.590 --> 00:22:21.673
like, why don't you just go back to Hawaii?

596
00:22:21.673 --> 00:22:23.700
You're like I'm gonna go to Hong Kong now.

597
00:22:23.700 --> 00:22:25.293
I know, well, funnily enough,

598
00:22:27.560 --> 00:22:29.670
my friend was pissed off, same friend.

599
00:22:29.670 --> 00:22:32.240
She went to her agency and she said,

600
00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:34.620
I don't understand why Maggie's getting rejected

601
00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:36.470
on this level, like what's happening.

602
00:22:36.470 --> 00:22:38.970
And she said to her, she said, well, I'll tell you

603
00:22:38.970 --> 00:22:40.260
do you want to hear the truth?

604
00:22:40.260 --> 00:22:42.850
And she was like, yeah, I wanna help her.

605
00:22:42.850 --> 00:22:46.530
She said, the problem with Maggie is she's not cute,

606
00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:48.490
which is one thing we like in this market,

607
00:22:48.490 --> 00:22:49.990
and she's not beautiful.

608
00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:52.511
And that's another thing we like in this market.

609
00:22:52.511 --> 00:22:53.344
(Rich laughs)
They're like,

610
00:22:53.344 --> 00:22:54.520
she's neither.

611
00:22:54.520 --> 00:22:56.950
And so she falls between the cracks.

612
00:22:56.950 --> 00:23:00.400
And my friend was like, oh my God, how awful?

613
00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:01.233
And I ended up-

614
00:23:01.233 --> 00:23:02.910
It's such a terrible thing to say.

615
00:23:02.910 --> 00:23:03.870
Yeah, and she told me.

616
00:23:03.870 --> 00:23:04.788
And I was like

617
00:23:04.788 --> 00:23:07.790
I don't think I'm those things either.

618
00:23:07.790 --> 00:23:09.800
I hate this industry.

619
00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:11.393
It's so terrible.

620
00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:14.670
Drives girls to the brink of insanity.

621
00:23:14.670 --> 00:23:15.610
I don't wanna do this.

622
00:23:15.610 --> 00:23:17.980
I just want to go to school and like be an athlete.

623
00:23:17.980 --> 00:23:19.620
And like, that's what I wanted to do,

624
00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:21.340
but I just didn't have the money to do it.

625
00:23:21.340 --> 00:23:23.920
So I was like, they're not telling me,

626
00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:25.090
so I'm not heartbroken.

627
00:23:25.090 --> 00:23:27.830
I don't wanna be a model, it sucks, this is awful.

628
00:23:27.830 --> 00:23:30.310
Like, you know, I wouldn't recommend it.

629
00:23:30.310 --> 00:23:33.008
I know you have two daughters I don't recommend it (laughs)-

630
00:23:33.008 --> 00:23:35.800
And now next stop Hong Kong-
Our next stop Hong Kong.

631
00:23:35.800 --> 00:23:38.170
But funnily enough, like I get to Hong Kong,

632
00:23:38.170 --> 00:23:41.680
and I sort of like did use the word modeling very loosely.

633
00:23:41.680 --> 00:23:44.650
I mean, I did commercial work, things like that.

634
00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:46.690
And then within that year,

635
00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:49.130
at the time Jackie Chan, had a management company,

636
00:23:49.130 --> 00:23:51.320
where he was sort of looking for the next generation

637
00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:52.160
of action stars.

638
00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:53.350
Like that's what he was doing.

639
00:23:53.350 --> 00:23:57.070
And he knew that his name and his, you know,

640
00:23:57.070 --> 00:24:02.070
all the things would be a great sort of headline,

641
00:24:02.160 --> 00:24:03.170
to what he was doing.

642
00:24:03.170 --> 00:24:05.880
And he was, kind of training all these young boys,

643
00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:08.860
and like, I was like the girl and they took me on,

644
00:24:08.860 --> 00:24:10.830
and they trained me.

645
00:24:10.830 --> 00:24:15.158
His team trained me and I became this sort of like action-

646
00:24:15.158 --> 00:24:15.991
Right.

647
00:24:15.991 --> 00:24:18.187
So you just blew up in Asia

648
00:24:18.187 --> 00:24:22.290
and it's hard to imagine how big Jackie Chan was in Asia

649
00:24:22.290 --> 00:24:24.290
at that time, and probably still, right?

650
00:24:24.290 --> 00:24:25.123
Yeah.

651
00:24:25.123 --> 00:24:28.920
And in America, cause like he had already hit here

652
00:24:28.920 --> 00:24:30.450
and he was huge.

653
00:24:30.450 --> 00:24:32.880
So he'd become this global superstar.

654
00:24:32.880 --> 00:24:35.070
And then in his backyard,

655
00:24:35.070 --> 00:24:37.320
he wanted to create another business.

656
00:24:37.320 --> 00:24:39.470
And the business was training these young people

657
00:24:39.470 --> 00:24:41.152
and creating the new generation of action stars.

658
00:24:41.152 --> 00:24:43.724
And then just becoming more of a producer.

659
00:24:43.724 --> 00:24:45.480
And becoming more of a producer in that respect,

660
00:24:45.480 --> 00:24:46.990
and still starring in what he was doing.

661
00:24:46.990 --> 00:24:48.770
But not necessarily, you know

662
00:24:48.770 --> 00:24:50.540
we were starring in these smaller movies

663
00:24:50.540 --> 00:24:52.290
and he was still doing his big stuff (chuckles).

664
00:24:52.290 --> 00:24:56.520
So you kind of go to like action movie star university.

665
00:24:56.520 --> 00:24:58.720
Like you get trained in martial arts,

666
00:24:58.720 --> 00:25:02.542
and become this badass warrior for the screen.

667
00:25:02.542 --> 00:25:04.960
And I was a runner, okay?

668
00:25:04.960 --> 00:25:07.280
So you have to understand like people who aren't runners,

669
00:25:07.280 --> 00:25:09.620
like we're not flexible people.

670
00:25:09.620 --> 00:25:12.110
Like I couldn't touch my toes at the time, you know?

671
00:25:12.110 --> 00:25:12.980
And they're sort of looking at me

672
00:25:12.980 --> 00:25:16.100
and going, ah, you look strong and we think you are strong

673
00:25:16.100 --> 00:25:17.920
and we think we can make you into something,

674
00:25:17.920 --> 00:25:20.160
but jeez, like it's gonna take a while

675
00:25:20.160 --> 00:25:21.930
So what was that process like?

676
00:25:21.930 --> 00:25:23.210
Like what do they have you doing?

677
00:25:23.210 --> 00:25:26.182
Well, Jackie has a team of like 10, anywhere from like 10

678
00:25:26.182 --> 00:25:29.620
to 15 people who are with him at all times.

679
00:25:29.620 --> 00:25:33.226
And this is his team of like martial artists.

680
00:25:33.226 --> 00:25:34.850
And these are the same people that fight with him

681
00:25:34.850 --> 00:25:35.970
in all the movies, right?
In all the movies.

682
00:25:35.970 --> 00:25:37.610
So, like when I watch Jackie's movies.

683
00:25:37.610 --> 00:25:39.330
I know every single person he's fighting.

684
00:25:39.330 --> 00:25:41.221
Because I know them all, right?

685
00:25:41.221 --> 00:25:42.303
Right, it's the same dudes (laughs)

686
00:25:42.303 --> 00:25:43.303
And people don't understand,

687
00:25:43.303 --> 00:25:45.330
like you can't just throw someone in a fight

688
00:25:45.330 --> 00:25:46.163
with Jackie Chan.

689
00:25:46.163 --> 00:25:46.996
He's too good.

690
00:25:46.996 --> 00:25:49.540
So you have to know him and be able to fight him.

691
00:25:49.540 --> 00:25:52.380
So basically like his team moves with him

692
00:25:52.380 --> 00:25:54.440
and every movie he's in, if there's a villain,

693
00:25:54.440 --> 00:25:56.540
like they have to plug in his guy.

694
00:25:56.540 --> 00:25:58.130
They're the only people who can find him.

695
00:25:58.130 --> 00:25:59.140
Wow.

696
00:25:59.140 --> 00:26:00.223
So what is the tradition?

697
00:26:00.223 --> 00:26:03.682
Like the martial arts tradition that they indoctrinate you-

698
00:26:03.682 --> 00:26:05.620
So those are the guys that train you, like his team.

699
00:26:05.620 --> 00:26:08.060
And they're specialist in every discipline.

700
00:26:08.060 --> 00:26:10.270
So he's got like the Kung Fu guy, the TaeKwonDo guy,

701
00:26:10.270 --> 00:26:12.490
the karate guy, like everybody is specialized.

702
00:26:12.490 --> 00:26:17.490
And so they sort of take you on and they, they break you.

703
00:26:19.750 --> 00:26:21.891
I mean they break, I don't know (laughs).

704
00:26:21.891 --> 00:26:23.620
So what's the pitch, they're like Maggie,

705
00:26:23.620 --> 00:26:27.070
okay, here's the upside opportunity you're gonna be in

706
00:26:27.070 --> 00:26:28.690
all these movies-
No, that conversation,

707
00:26:28.690 --> 00:26:29.633
never happens.

708
00:26:30.560 --> 00:26:33.429
So that's a very Western thing that you're...

709
00:26:33.429 --> 00:26:36.860
So everything you're saying makes sense in a logical world,

710
00:26:36.860 --> 00:26:39.760
and then you're in Asia and nothing makes sense.

711
00:26:39.760 --> 00:26:43.390
So they don't give you any foresight

712
00:26:43.390 --> 00:26:45.900
like where you're gonna head or what's gonna happen.

713
00:26:45.900 --> 00:26:49.300
It's basically like, here, let's break you first,

714
00:26:49.300 --> 00:26:52.080
see how good you are, and if you're actually good

715
00:26:52.080 --> 00:26:54.130
then we'll see where it goes kind of thing.

716
00:26:54.130 --> 00:26:55.880
And are they paying you, and supporting you,

717
00:26:55.880 --> 00:26:56.961
in the meantime?

718
00:26:56.961 --> 00:27:00.730
No, I mean, I was feeding myself through like commercials

719
00:27:00.730 --> 00:27:02.145
and things like that.

720
00:27:02.145 --> 00:27:04.470
So you got an agent or, I mean, how does it work?

721
00:27:04.470 --> 00:27:08.140
Like what's the parallel, or the disconnect between

722
00:27:08.140 --> 00:27:11.300
like the Hong Kong version of Hollywood and like Hollywood?

723
00:27:11.300 --> 00:27:14.490
Well, there's no unions, there's no agents.

724
00:27:14.490 --> 00:27:16.790
There's no publicists, none of that.

725
00:27:16.790 --> 00:27:19.000
None of what exists here, is there.

726
00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:20.470
I mean you have a manager,

727
00:27:20.470 --> 00:27:23.740
and that person handles absolutely everything you do.

728
00:27:23.740 --> 00:27:26.510
They're, like your life basically.

729
00:27:26.510 --> 00:27:28.610
But they don't specialize in all those things.

730
00:27:28.610 --> 00:27:30.630
So, you know, there's no protections.

731
00:27:30.630 --> 00:27:33.500
I mean, there was a time I was on set for like 30 hours

732
00:27:33.500 --> 00:27:35.670
and there was no, nobody said,

733
00:27:35.670 --> 00:27:37.661
okay we should probably go back and sleep now.

734
00:27:37.661 --> 00:27:39.040
And there was no one to call.

735
00:27:39.040 --> 00:27:40.853
There's no like union hotline-

736
00:27:40.853 --> 00:27:44.430
And you've been doing martial arts and justifying stunts-

737
00:27:44.430 --> 00:27:46.550
Right, and tired out of your mind,

738
00:27:46.550 --> 00:27:49.100
like really, truly is like a form of torture,

739
00:27:49.100 --> 00:27:52.050
where you're like the level of physicality is so high

740
00:27:52.050 --> 00:27:54.280
and yet you're just under-resourced in every way,

741
00:27:54.280 --> 00:27:56.140
you're tired, you're not getting the right food.

742
00:27:56.140 --> 00:27:57.170
You're not eating, the whole thing.

743
00:27:57.170 --> 00:27:59.700
So it's sort of like, the early days of Hollywood,

744
00:27:59.700 --> 00:28:03.650
where the actor was sort of employed by the studio system,

745
00:28:03.650 --> 00:28:06.585
you go here, and you're getting your pittance of a wage.

746
00:28:06.585 --> 00:28:09.327
100%, I would say that, yes.

747
00:28:09.327 --> 00:28:11.000
And at least being with Jackie,

748
00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:13.390
I had some sort of protection against,

749
00:28:14.605 --> 00:28:17.577
I think it was a protection against a lot of, that studio,

750
00:28:19.920 --> 00:28:22.740
mafioso type of stuff that they do,

751
00:28:22.740 --> 00:28:24.970
in all parts of the world, but over there, especially,

752
00:28:24.970 --> 00:28:27.500
it's sort of like, I was his girl

753
00:28:27.500 --> 00:28:29.680
and that I was like someone he was bringing up,

754
00:28:29.680 --> 00:28:31.200
that he was raising in the business.

755
00:28:31.200 --> 00:28:34.540
So I wasn't to be messed with too much.

756
00:28:34.540 --> 00:28:35.373
You know what I mean?

757
00:28:35.373 --> 00:28:37.430
Like there was sort of a blanket of protection a little bit.

758
00:28:37.430 --> 00:28:38.920
So that helped me a lot.

759
00:28:38.920 --> 00:28:39.753
Right.

760
00:28:39.753 --> 00:28:41.660
So you survive all this and you end up,

761
00:28:41.660 --> 00:28:44.810
I mean you are under his wing, right?

762
00:28:44.810 --> 00:28:49.014
So this like blows you up into this massive star in Asia.

763
00:28:49.014 --> 00:28:49.847
Yeah.

764
00:28:49.847 --> 00:28:51.240
I was listening to the podcasts that you did

765
00:28:51.240 --> 00:28:52.880
with Justin Long.
Oh, yeah.

766
00:28:52.880 --> 00:28:56.720
And he was like, just expressing like how amazing it was

767
00:28:56.720 --> 00:29:00.130
to like discover like what a big deal you are in Asia.

768
00:29:00.130 --> 00:29:02.910
Well, we went to, cause we did die hard together, right?

769
00:29:02.910 --> 00:29:05.390
So we go to like, you know they sent us

770
00:29:05.390 --> 00:29:06.237
to different places and stuff.

771
00:29:06.237 --> 00:29:08.170
And so I go to a...

772
00:29:08.170 --> 00:29:10.200
You know we're doing this junket and then Bruce's somewhere,

773
00:29:10.200 --> 00:29:12.240
and then Justin and I were somewhere else

774
00:29:12.240 --> 00:29:14.160
and we walked, I think we were in Singapore,

775
00:29:14.160 --> 00:29:15.740
and they had like hubbed Singapore,

776
00:29:15.740 --> 00:29:17.890
as like all the Asian press had to come down there,

777
00:29:17.890 --> 00:29:19.140
'cause we didn't have this kind of time.

778
00:29:19.140 --> 00:29:20.250
We had a premiere in Tokyo,

779
00:29:20.250 --> 00:29:21.360
and then went straight down to Singapore,

780
00:29:21.360 --> 00:29:23.951
and then we had to go to the World Premiere In Berlin.

781
00:29:23.951 --> 00:29:24.814
(chuckles)

782
00:29:24.814 --> 00:29:26.070
And I remember like we walked to this place,

783
00:29:26.070 --> 00:29:30.454
and he looks around and he's like, holy crap,

784
00:29:30.454 --> 00:29:33.380
all of the posters are you.

785
00:29:33.380 --> 00:29:34.920
Like, you know how you see the Die Hard poster,

786
00:29:34.920 --> 00:29:37.491
and you're like Bruce (indistinct)

787
00:29:37.491 --> 00:29:39.820
you know those small eyes, sort of thing that he does,

788
00:29:39.820 --> 00:29:41.630
the winky winky.

789
00:29:41.630 --> 00:29:42.463
And they were me.

790
00:29:42.463 --> 00:29:46.430
And he was like, oh, my God, like, what's happening?

791
00:29:46.430 --> 00:29:47.740
Like, how come he's not up here?

792
00:29:47.740 --> 00:29:49.720
I'm like, (murmurs), he's like, is he not big here.

793
00:29:49.720 --> 00:29:50.570
I'm like, he's huge here.

794
00:29:50.570 --> 00:29:54.000
And they're like, but he couldn't wrap his head around it.

795
00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:55.070
He thought it was the funniest.

796
00:29:55.070 --> 00:29:57.250
Right, yeah.
(Maggie laughs)

797
00:29:57.250 --> 00:30:01.450
And is it like, I'm trying to wrap my head around

798
00:30:01.450 --> 00:30:03.120
that experience being in Hong Kong,

799
00:30:03.120 --> 00:30:06.580
like is there the same, you know there's a premiere,

800
00:30:06.580 --> 00:30:08.990
and there's a red carpet, and there's paparazzi,

801
00:30:08.990 --> 00:30:10.090
and there's magazines.

802
00:30:10.090 --> 00:30:13.230
And like, how does that whole like kind of infrastructure

803
00:30:13.230 --> 00:30:16.940
around the film industry operate to like create stars

804
00:30:16.940 --> 00:30:17.892
and all of that?

805
00:30:17.892 --> 00:30:21.830
It's very unruly, I have to say, like there was a period

806
00:30:21.830 --> 00:30:24.490
of like two years before I actually left Hong Kong,

807
00:30:24.490 --> 00:30:26.523
and got my first film here in the US.

808
00:30:27.786 --> 00:30:31.420
I didn't wanna be in this industry anymore.

809
00:30:31.420 --> 00:30:34.940
To me, it wasn't something that was worth it,

810
00:30:34.940 --> 00:30:37.700
because the paparazzi issue was so bad,

811
00:30:37.700 --> 00:30:41.510
and the invasiveness it was so awful

812
00:30:41.510 --> 00:30:43.690
like to the point where, I mean, for me,

813
00:30:43.690 --> 00:30:46.310
like, I'm a woman who looks a certain way.

814
00:30:46.310 --> 00:30:48.900
And so in that region you get targeted for different things.

815
00:30:48.900 --> 00:30:53.900
So I had, been having trouble, you know, in the media,

816
00:30:54.070 --> 00:30:55.940
cause I had a relationship that ended

817
00:30:55.940 --> 00:30:57.560
and they were like, oh, it must be her fault.

818
00:30:57.560 --> 00:30:58.393
She must be evil.

819
00:30:58.393 --> 00:30:59.830
She must be that, all this sort of stuff.

820
00:30:59.830 --> 00:31:02.090
So they're like, don't go out, please don't go out.

821
00:31:02.090 --> 00:31:03.950
Just stay home and let this blow over.

822
00:31:03.950 --> 00:31:05.030
I'm like, oh whatever.

823
00:31:05.030 --> 00:31:06.580
So I'm at home and I have a friend call me

824
00:31:06.580 --> 00:31:08.760
and he says, hey, we're out on the water today,

825
00:31:08.760 --> 00:31:09.593
it's so beautiful.

826
00:31:09.593 --> 00:31:10.426
You gotta come out of the house.

827
00:31:10.426 --> 00:31:11.630
I was instructed not to leave my house.

828
00:31:11.630 --> 00:31:13.330
I'm not allowed to leave my house.

829
00:31:13.330 --> 00:31:14.820
My friend says Maggie, were on the boat

830
00:31:14.820 --> 00:31:15.653
in the middle of nowhere.

831
00:31:15.653 --> 00:31:18.080
Like, you know, please come out

832
00:31:18.080 --> 00:31:20.100
like, I mean please you're stressed, like just come.

833
00:31:20.100 --> 00:31:22.340
Like it's just us and we're just gonna hang out.

834
00:31:22.340 --> 00:31:26.300
So I sneak in a taxi and literally had to call the taxi

835
00:31:26.300 --> 00:31:27.133
into the parking garage.

836
00:31:27.133 --> 00:31:29.730
I laid down in the back seat, cause they're just sitting

837
00:31:29.730 --> 00:31:30.720
outside of my house.

838
00:31:30.720 --> 00:31:33.680
So I get to the thing, I evade them.

839
00:31:33.680 --> 00:31:34.900
I get into this little dinghy.

840
00:31:34.900 --> 00:31:35.733
I get to this boat.

841
00:31:35.733 --> 00:31:38.150
I see my couple of friends of mine that I know I'm so happy,

842
00:31:38.150 --> 00:31:38.983
it's sunny.

843
00:31:38.983 --> 00:31:40.820
I'm like, oh, this is so great.

844
00:31:40.820 --> 00:31:44.180
And then four days later, I'm walking by a newsstand

845
00:31:44.180 --> 00:31:45.480
and there's this magazine.

846
00:31:45.480 --> 00:31:47.810
And it says in Chinese,

847
00:31:47.810 --> 00:31:51.598
Maggie doesn't get out of bed for less than 200 million.

848
00:31:51.598 --> 00:31:54.130
(Rich laughs)
What in God's name?

849
00:31:54.130 --> 00:31:55.970
And then there's a picture of the boat,

850
00:31:55.970 --> 00:31:57.853
and there's these telephoto lenses.

851
00:31:58.690 --> 00:32:00.180
And they caught me on this boat.

852
00:32:00.180 --> 00:32:02.102
I don't know whose boat it was,

853
00:32:02.102 --> 00:32:03.449
it's a Western friend of mine from Boston.

854
00:32:03.449 --> 00:32:05.900
It's some big fancy boat.
Yeah, I guess

855
00:32:05.900 --> 00:32:09.040
the person who owned it, I didn't even know who he was.

856
00:32:09.040 --> 00:32:10.903
I guess I had passed him on the deck.

857
00:32:11.910 --> 00:32:13.010
I never met him in my life.

858
00:32:13.010 --> 00:32:14.990
Passed him on the deck, go say hi to my friends.

859
00:32:14.990 --> 00:32:16.850
And they got that photo of us passing each other.

860
00:32:16.850 --> 00:32:19.446
And then it was just this three months attack, attack.

861
00:32:19.446 --> 00:32:21.700
So, it's basically saying you're in a relationship

862
00:32:21.700 --> 00:32:23.470
with this person.
Yeah, no, 100%.

863
00:32:23.470 --> 00:32:26.430
That I was, or that I'm some kind of high class hooker

864
00:32:26.430 --> 00:32:28.360
you know sort of like is in this relationship.

865
00:32:28.360 --> 00:32:29.240
And I'm like, really?

866
00:32:29.240 --> 00:32:33.049
I take taxis everywhere, I mean, what lifestyle,

867
00:32:33.049 --> 00:32:35.477
is it that you're trying to prove that I live.

868
00:32:35.477 --> 00:32:36.310
That's intense.

869
00:32:36.310 --> 00:32:38.600
So this is what, like early 2000's?

870
00:32:38.600 --> 00:32:39.433
It was sort of, 2000.

871
00:32:39.433 --> 00:32:41.510
It was so gross,

872
00:32:41.510 --> 00:32:44.343
that I was just like, this is not worth it to me.

873
00:32:45.233 --> 00:32:49.000
I mean, I don't typically ever seek attention anyway.

874
00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:50.280
I'm really not that person,

875
00:32:50.280 --> 00:32:52.010
like even here, I'mma I do my work and I go home.

876
00:32:52.010 --> 00:32:53.850
I really am like that boring (laughs).

877
00:32:53.850 --> 00:32:58.530
Was that a big part of the impetus to leave and come back

878
00:32:58.530 --> 00:32:59.550
to the States?

879
00:32:59.550 --> 00:33:04.550
I kind of knew that somewhere, I was heading back this way

880
00:33:06.320 --> 00:33:08.833
because I couldn't take it anymore anyway.

881
00:33:11.000 --> 00:33:12.670
But I was in a complicated situation,

882
00:33:12.670 --> 00:33:15.090
because I got Mission Impossible.

883
00:33:15.090 --> 00:33:18.360
And I was going back to the States in 2005,

884
00:33:18.360 --> 00:33:20.300
but my best friend was dying at the time.

885
00:33:20.300 --> 00:33:23.020
She was very ill and she was living there.

886
00:33:23.020 --> 00:33:27.370
And so I just sort of had this thing where I got this break

887
00:33:27.370 --> 00:33:29.860
but then the person I love the most in this world,

888
00:33:29.860 --> 00:33:30.840
was not well.

889
00:33:30.840 --> 00:33:33.130
I had been taking care of her already for two years,

890
00:33:33.130 --> 00:33:35.620
and now I had to go and do this movie.

891
00:33:35.620 --> 00:33:38.670
And she was always this like oberweis,

892
00:33:38.670 --> 00:33:40.760
kind of sagey human being.

893
00:33:40.760 --> 00:33:42.380
And all right I got the film

894
00:33:42.380 --> 00:33:44.420
and I had to say goodbye to her to go to this movie.

895
00:33:44.420 --> 00:33:46.190
But I was like, I'm only gonna be gone X amount of months,

896
00:33:46.190 --> 00:33:47.280
and then we'll be back.

897
00:33:47.280 --> 00:33:48.550
We'll be back, and I'm gonna take care of you,

898
00:33:48.550 --> 00:33:49.570
and I'm not leaving.

899
00:33:49.570 --> 00:33:51.060
I'm not leaving you.

900
00:33:51.060 --> 00:33:54.697
And she looked at me and she was like,

901
00:33:54.697 --> 00:33:56.549
you're not coming back?

902
00:33:56.549 --> 00:33:59.848
And I was like, no, no, no, of course I'm coming back.

903
00:33:59.848 --> 00:34:03.330
And she was like, Maggie, you don't belong here.

904
00:34:03.330 --> 00:34:05.020
I don't want you back.

905
00:34:05.020 --> 00:34:06.640
You belong over there.

906
00:34:06.640 --> 00:34:08.150
You need to be doing the things,

907
00:34:08.150 --> 00:34:10.450
that you're meant to be doing, and it's not here.

908
00:34:10.450 --> 00:34:13.510
And it was a weird thing when she said that,

909
00:34:13.510 --> 00:34:16.820
because it hit me, and it scared me,

910
00:34:16.820 --> 00:34:18.990
that I'd come back and she wouldn't be there-

911
00:34:18.990 --> 00:34:21.600
Right, but what a beautiful gift.

912
00:34:21.600 --> 00:34:24.954
What a beautiful gift, truly and then I was on the movie-

913
00:34:24.954 --> 00:34:26.542
Did she pass when you were...

914
00:34:26.542 --> 00:34:27.680
On the movie.
Wow.

915
00:34:27.680 --> 00:34:28.513
And I knew.

916
00:34:28.513 --> 00:34:29.390
I knew she was going do that.

917
00:34:29.390 --> 00:34:30.223
I just knew it.

918
00:34:30.223 --> 00:34:32.410
I knew that she was gonna let go, while I was gone

919
00:34:32.410 --> 00:34:36.540
because I knew, that she knew I would have come back.

920
00:34:36.540 --> 00:34:38.081
She just did.
Wow.

921
00:34:38.081 --> 00:34:41.690
Yeah, and she didn't want that and told me as such and so.

922
00:34:41.690 --> 00:34:42.910
Yeah.
Yeah-

923
00:34:42.910 --> 00:34:45.310
But that also, gave you the ability

924
00:34:45.310 --> 00:34:47.080
to have that clean break.

925
00:34:47.080 --> 00:34:50.870
It did, and it was really funny because public perception

926
00:34:50.870 --> 00:34:52.410
versus what it is that you deal with.

927
00:34:52.410 --> 00:34:54.310
I couldn't go back to Hong Kong for years,

928
00:34:54.310 --> 00:34:56.050
'cause I was in a lot of pain over that.

929
00:34:56.050 --> 00:34:58.250
And I couldn't even go back for her funeral.

930
00:34:58.250 --> 00:34:59.470
Like the schedule didn't allow me.

931
00:34:59.470 --> 00:35:01.500
I couldn't even go back and say goodbye.

932
00:35:01.500 --> 00:35:03.700
So it was, and it's not my movie, right?

933
00:35:03.700 --> 00:35:04.860
It's Tom Cruise's movie.

934
00:35:04.860 --> 00:35:06.750
Like I don't walk into the production office

935
00:35:06.750 --> 00:35:08.470
and go, hey, can you do me a huge favor?

936
00:35:08.470 --> 00:35:10.170
I'm number nine on the call sheet, you know.

937
00:35:10.170 --> 00:35:12.750
But in Asia, did the posters all have you on them

938
00:35:12.750 --> 00:35:13.730
instead of Tom cruise?

939
00:35:13.730 --> 00:35:17.700
No, they had all of us, (laughs).

940
00:35:17.700 --> 00:35:21.260
Well, there's so much here-
(indistinct) Tom cruise.

941
00:35:21.260 --> 00:35:23.560
First of all, it's absolutely bananas

942
00:35:23.560 --> 00:35:27.050
that the first American movie that you book

943
00:35:27.050 --> 00:35:29.560
is Mission Impossible, with Tom Cruise and J.J.Abrams.

944
00:35:29.560 --> 00:35:31.827
I mean, that's insane right?
Absolutely insane.

945
00:35:31.827 --> 00:35:33.020
And I wanna get to that,

946
00:35:33.020 --> 00:35:36.490
but first I wanna spend a couple of minutes on Jackie Chan

947
00:35:36.490 --> 00:35:39.040
still who's the Tom cruise of Asia, right?

948
00:35:39.040 --> 00:35:40.953
Like there's a lot of similarities.

949
00:35:40.953 --> 00:35:44.210
I mean, this guy is like a perfectionist bar none, right?

950
00:35:44.210 --> 00:35:47.690
I Have said that to everyone, who's asked me about it.

951
00:35:47.690 --> 00:35:51.310
I'm like, there's no one who works harder than Tom cruise

952
00:35:51.310 --> 00:35:54.400
or Jackie Chan, on different sides of the same work ethic.

953
00:35:54.400 --> 00:35:57.830
Same just tenacity, same leadership skills.

954
00:35:57.830 --> 00:36:00.690
I mean, they're very similar, in that respect.

955
00:36:00.690 --> 00:36:01.523
Right.
Yeah.

956
00:36:01.523 --> 00:36:03.300
So what did you learn?

957
00:36:03.300 --> 00:36:06.900
So I would imagine the bootcamp under Jackie and his team,

958
00:36:06.900 --> 00:36:10.090
like really sorted you out and made you prepare.

959
00:36:10.090 --> 00:36:14.130
Like it's crazy, like looking back in the rear view mirror

960
00:36:14.130 --> 00:36:15.913
that it all lined up like that,

961
00:36:15.913 --> 00:36:18.420
like had you not trained under Jackie,

962
00:36:18.420 --> 00:36:20.440
you wouldn't have been able to manage Tom cruise.

963
00:36:20.440 --> 00:36:21.807
I would imagine, (laughs)

964
00:36:21.807 --> 00:36:24.210
like that would have just been an energy blast

965
00:36:24.210 --> 00:36:25.160
A thousand percent correct.

966
00:36:25.160 --> 00:36:26.013
But also,

967
00:36:27.368 --> 00:36:28.660
I had a work ethic,

968
00:36:28.660 --> 00:36:30.750
I think that was just second to none.

969
00:36:30.750 --> 00:36:33.530
Like over there, there are no breaks.

970
00:36:33.530 --> 00:36:35.010
There are no compliments.

971
00:36:35.010 --> 00:36:37.410
There is no encouragement.

972
00:36:37.410 --> 00:36:38.980
It's like you either get the job done,

973
00:36:38.980 --> 00:36:42.250
or you don't, you know, you're completely out.

974
00:36:42.250 --> 00:36:47.020
And I was on sets where like, you know, I had three or four,

975
00:36:47.020 --> 00:36:49.340
different stunt women at the same time,

976
00:36:49.340 --> 00:36:52.820
because not one of them was skilled enough to cover me

977
00:36:52.820 --> 00:36:55.560
in different bases and-

978
00:36:55.560 --> 00:36:56.568
In Hong Kong, or on Mission Impossible?

979
00:36:56.568 --> 00:36:57.480
In Hong Kong.
In Hong Kong.

980
00:36:57.480 --> 00:36:59.210
That we're just getting screamed off set,

981
00:36:59.210 --> 00:37:01.610
and fired, left, right and center.

982
00:37:01.610 --> 00:37:03.260
I mean, these are professional stunt women

983
00:37:03.260 --> 00:37:05.130
where the director is yelling at them and saying,

984
00:37:05.130 --> 00:37:08.360
if you're not better than the actress, get off my set.

985
00:37:08.360 --> 00:37:09.568
And I mean, it's like that.

986
00:37:09.568 --> 00:37:11.630
I mean, it's, it's (indistinct), it's crazy.

987
00:37:11.630 --> 00:37:14.990
So the training prepared me,

988
00:37:14.990 --> 00:37:18.170
not just for the level of physicality that I would face

989
00:37:18.170 --> 00:37:19.270
when I got to the States,

990
00:37:19.270 --> 00:37:23.130
but also just the discipline, and the work ethic,

991
00:37:23.130 --> 00:37:26.130
to be able to just continue to push through

992
00:37:26.130 --> 00:37:27.310
until the job is done right.

993
00:37:27.310 --> 00:37:28.270
Right.

994
00:37:28.270 --> 00:37:31.550
And there's not a lot of people with that work ethic.

995
00:37:31.550 --> 00:37:32.495
Yeah.

996
00:37:32.495 --> 00:37:34.559
(chuckles)

997
00:37:34.559 --> 00:37:37.650
I mean, we all heard that, Tom cruise

998
00:37:37.650 --> 00:37:40.028
outburst of whatever movie he was on,

999
00:37:40.028 --> 00:37:41.840
where they're trying to shoot on COVID,

1000
00:37:41.840 --> 00:37:42.710
and he got all pissed off

1001
00:37:42.710 --> 00:37:44.240
because people weren't following protocols.

1002
00:37:44.240 --> 00:37:47.250
And it's like, he's the producer, he's the star,

1003
00:37:47.250 --> 00:37:50.160
he's trying to make sure the ship is moving

1004
00:37:50.160 --> 00:37:51.580
and everybody has a job-

1005
00:37:51.580 --> 00:37:53.168
He has every right.

1006
00:37:53.168 --> 00:37:56.107
So I heard that and I was lucky for him.

1007
00:37:56.107 --> 00:37:58.000
And also because I know him.

1008
00:37:58.000 --> 00:38:01.240
I know how fair he is in the professional realm.

1009
00:38:01.240 --> 00:38:03.530
Like I obviously, I don't know him outside

1010
00:38:03.530 --> 00:38:05.900
of the professional realm, besides his like house-warming

1011
00:38:05.900 --> 00:38:07.350
but like outside of that,

1012
00:38:07.350 --> 00:38:08.770
I'm not like, you know what I mean.

1013
00:38:08.770 --> 00:38:13.240
On that level, but as a professional, he's fair.

1014
00:38:13.240 --> 00:38:15.110
You know, he comes to work and he's like,

1015
00:38:15.110 --> 00:38:16.330
I want everything to work,

1016
00:38:16.330 --> 00:38:17.430
and I wanna provide for (murmurs).

1017
00:38:17.430 --> 00:38:19.160
He's a provider.
Yeah.

1018
00:38:19.160 --> 00:38:20.522
You know what I mean?

1019
00:38:20.522 --> 00:38:22.100
I'm sure if you did the math,

1020
00:38:22.100 --> 00:38:24.370
I mean, he's responsible for, you know, (chuckles)

1021
00:38:24.370 --> 00:38:25.690
a lot of what the industry makes.

1022
00:38:25.690 --> 00:38:28.170
Of course, he sets the bar incredibly high,

1023
00:38:28.170 --> 00:38:30.040
and then he outworks everybody else.

1024
00:38:30.040 --> 00:38:32.527
And at the same time, it's hard to connect with it.

1025
00:38:32.527 --> 00:38:34.540
You're like, is this guy a human being,

1026
00:38:34.540 --> 00:38:36.954
or is he like from a different planet, right?

1027
00:38:36.954 --> 00:38:38.090
Like, what is the experience,

1028
00:38:38.090 --> 00:38:40.500
of actually working with that guy?

1029
00:38:40.500 --> 00:38:42.560
You know, he...

1030
00:38:42.560 --> 00:38:43.430
Okay, there's two things.

1031
00:38:43.430 --> 00:38:47.210
One, he has an enthusiasm, like no one I've ever met

1032
00:38:47.210 --> 00:38:48.094
in my life.

1033
00:38:48.094 --> 00:38:50.620
Like it just seems almost it's so off the chain

1034
00:38:50.620 --> 00:38:53.697
that it feels like, is this manufactured, or is this real?

1035
00:38:53.697 --> 00:38:56.040
And you're like, I don't think it's real with this guy.

1036
00:38:56.040 --> 00:38:57.020
How does he maintain that, (laughs).

1037
00:38:57.020 --> 00:38:58.270
Well, when I go to the States,

1038
00:38:58.270 --> 00:39:01.390
I didn't know any of the who ha around his new relationship

1039
00:39:01.390 --> 00:39:02.840
like all that stuff in 2005.

1040
00:39:02.840 --> 00:39:05.560
Like I just didn't, because I wasn't following it.

1041
00:39:05.560 --> 00:39:06.540
And I was on the other side of the world.

1042
00:39:06.540 --> 00:39:10.290
And so I got back and it was like, it was Kerry Russell

1043
00:39:10.290 --> 00:39:11.430
who I did Mission with,

1044
00:39:11.430 --> 00:39:13.410
where I was like, what's happening here?

1045
00:39:13.410 --> 00:39:15.830
Like, who's the girl and then she's like,

1046
00:39:15.830 --> 00:39:18.290
oh you don't know about Oprah on the couch jumping (murmurs)

1047
00:39:18.290 --> 00:39:19.673
and I'm like, no, my God,

1048
00:39:19.673 --> 00:39:21.780
what is this thing you're talking about?

1049
00:39:21.780 --> 00:39:24.210
So we go to lunch, and she explains to me like,

1050
00:39:24.210 --> 00:39:25.270
there's this new relationship?

1051
00:39:25.270 --> 00:39:27.200
And he's like jumping all over couches

1052
00:39:27.200 --> 00:39:28.033
and all that sort of stuff.

1053
00:39:28.033 --> 00:39:29.960
And I was like, oh, well, maybe he's just excited.

1054
00:39:29.960 --> 00:39:31.000
She's like, I don't know, Maggie.

1055
00:39:31.000 --> 00:39:33.077
There's like speculation I'm like, oh, this is weird.

1056
00:39:33.077 --> 00:39:35.470
And then, you know, as we got into,

1057
00:39:35.470 --> 00:39:38.910
when we started working like that enthusiasm,

1058
00:39:38.910 --> 00:39:40.420
later once I knew him,

1059
00:39:40.420 --> 00:39:42.600
I was sort of like, I looked at the couch jumping thing

1060
00:39:42.600 --> 00:39:44.940
with new eyes and I went, no, that's him.

1061
00:39:44.940 --> 00:39:47.220
He does stuff like that all the time.

1062
00:39:47.220 --> 00:39:48.970
Like, that's not over the top.
(Rich laughs)

1063
00:39:48.970 --> 00:39:49.950
That's what he does.

1064
00:39:49.950 --> 00:39:51.910
Like we're in Rome, and we're filming

1065
00:39:51.910 --> 00:39:53.722
and door bursts open and he's like,

1066
00:39:53.722 --> 00:39:54.580
(speaks in foreign language).

1067
00:39:54.580 --> 00:39:58.350
And he's so freaking excited about the day.

1068
00:39:58.350 --> 00:39:59.810
And that was every day.

1069
00:39:59.810 --> 00:40:00.643
It wasn't like-

1070
00:40:00.643 --> 00:40:01.930
So what is that?

1071
00:40:01.930 --> 00:40:03.275
Like, where's that coming from?

1072
00:40:03.275 --> 00:40:05.110
Like, what is that about?

1073
00:40:05.110 --> 00:40:09.360
I think that number one, he genuinely enjoys what he does.

1074
00:40:09.360 --> 00:40:11.054
And I think he still has fun doing it.

1075
00:40:11.054 --> 00:40:13.100
And I think at his level, (murmurs) (laughs).

1076
00:40:14.608 --> 00:40:17.830
But, I've worked with other A-listers,

1077
00:40:17.830 --> 00:40:21.610
you know, at his level, in terms of box office

1078
00:40:21.610 --> 00:40:22.870
and pay grade all that.

1079
00:40:22.870 --> 00:40:26.260
And they are not enthusiastic about coming to work.

1080
00:40:26.260 --> 00:40:28.130
So I wouldn't say it's the same

1081
00:40:28.130 --> 00:40:29.830
as other people at his level.

1082
00:40:29.830 --> 00:40:30.820
So that's special.

1083
00:40:30.820 --> 00:40:32.492
And then the other thing is,

1084
00:40:32.492 --> 00:40:37.492
I think that he knows that he is in a leadership position

1085
00:40:37.940 --> 00:40:40.960
that can change the tone,

1086
00:40:40.960 --> 00:40:44.930
or galvanize the tone on a set, like that.

1087
00:40:44.930 --> 00:40:46.300
And he's well aware of that.

1088
00:40:46.300 --> 00:40:48.760
And he's right, because I'm not Tom cruise

1089
00:40:48.760 --> 00:40:50.410
but I've been number one on my shows,

1090
00:40:50.410 --> 00:40:52.070
and things like that or movies.

1091
00:40:52.070 --> 00:40:53.920
And it is top-down.

1092
00:40:53.920 --> 00:40:56.900
I mean, if you come to set and you're that person,

1093
00:40:56.900 --> 00:40:59.637
everyone is affected by you, truly.

1094
00:40:59.637 --> 00:41:01.600
You know if you wanna give everyone a bad day,

1095
00:41:01.600 --> 00:41:02.710
you can absolutely do that.

1096
00:41:02.710 --> 00:41:03.630
Right.

1097
00:41:03.630 --> 00:41:08.313
But at the same time, like, what is he, 57 now-

1098
00:41:08.313 --> 00:41:10.301
Something like that.
56, something like that.

1099
00:41:10.301 --> 00:41:12.370
And you know, he's jumping from building to building,

1100
00:41:12.370 --> 00:41:14.920
and breaking his ankle, doing all these stunts.

1101
00:41:14.920 --> 00:41:18.300
And like, you know, it's just like the relentlessness-

1102
00:41:18.300 --> 00:41:19.133
It's relentless.

1103
00:41:19.133 --> 00:41:21.180
To achieve at the highest level,

1104
00:41:21.180 --> 00:41:24.569
is you know that engine inside of him is like something,

1105
00:41:24.569 --> 00:41:27.240
you just don't experience with almost anybody

1106
00:41:27.240 --> 00:41:28.073
you're ever gonna meet.

1107
00:41:28.073 --> 00:41:29.586
You just don't, you don't.

1108
00:41:29.586 --> 00:41:30.419
And he's been here, (chuckles)

1109
00:41:30.419 --> 00:41:33.540
he's like in decade five of doing this, or whatever.

1110
00:41:33.540 --> 00:41:35.660
And it's still, it's like a dynamo,

1111
00:41:35.660 --> 00:41:38.083
like it's a nuclear reactor-
It really is.

1112
00:41:38.083 --> 00:41:39.415
That never runs out of steam.

1113
00:41:39.415 --> 00:41:40.430
And he never runs out of steam.

1114
00:41:40.430 --> 00:41:44.090
I mean, it's almost inhuman what goes on with that person.

1115
00:41:44.090 --> 00:41:46.300
And I also can tell you from experience

1116
00:41:46.300 --> 00:41:48.350
that he does do everything.

1117
00:41:48.350 --> 00:41:51.280
and it's a lot of insurance to insure his movies.

1118
00:41:51.280 --> 00:41:52.113
Like he's-

1119
00:41:52.113 --> 00:41:56.190
There was all that footage of where he broke his ankle.

1120
00:41:56.190 --> 00:41:58.006
Like Mission, that leap.
Truly.

1121
00:41:58.006 --> 00:42:00.160
He doesn't have to do that.
Oh yeah, and easily done.

1122
00:42:00.160 --> 00:42:02.780
Like I'm telling you, like, I would get into like these

1123
00:42:02.780 --> 00:42:05.030
little arguments with JJ, about little things on Mission,

1124
00:42:05.030 --> 00:42:06.140
that he wouldn't let me do.

1125
00:42:06.140 --> 00:42:08.490
And I'm like, JJ, like I am capable,

1126
00:42:08.490 --> 00:42:11.590
and he's like, Maggie, I need you for the whole movie.

1127
00:42:11.590 --> 00:42:14.900
I can't lose you now we're in month one, it's stupid.

1128
00:42:14.900 --> 00:42:16.220
Like let's not take the risk.

1129
00:42:16.220 --> 00:42:18.430
And then my double, broke her ankle,

1130
00:42:18.430 --> 00:42:20.040
jumping off one balcony into another.

1131
00:42:20.040 --> 00:42:21.170
And he was just like,

1132
00:42:21.170 --> 00:42:23.988
it was that I told you so moment, (laughs)

1133
00:42:23.988 --> 00:42:26.389
He looked at me, and I'm like, okay, yeah (laughs).

1134
00:42:26.389 --> 00:42:28.150
(Rich laughs).
Right.

1135
00:42:28.150 --> 00:42:30.092
Well, yeah the story is,

1136
00:42:30.092 --> 00:42:32.620
and I don't know how much of this is true or apocryphal,

1137
00:42:32.620 --> 00:42:34.330
but you do your own stunts.

1138
00:42:34.330 --> 00:42:37.040
This is how you were trained in Hong Kong.

1139
00:42:37.040 --> 00:42:39.050
And how much of that is still the case.

1140
00:42:39.050 --> 00:42:42.780
I mean, short of JJ saying, I don't want you to do that.

1141
00:42:42.780 --> 00:42:45.060
Are you the person who's saying no, I'm gonna do that.

1142
00:42:45.060 --> 00:42:46.000
100%
Yeah.

1143
00:42:46.000 --> 00:42:48.210
And it's like a problem for some directors,

1144
00:42:48.210 --> 00:42:51.300
you know like they, for example-

1145
00:42:51.300 --> 00:42:52.800
Well it's a risk because if you get hurt,

1146
00:42:52.800 --> 00:42:53.633
they gotta shut down.

1147
00:42:53.633 --> 00:42:55.360
And this is it, and they're just like, Maggie,

1148
00:42:55.360 --> 00:42:57.040
I don't think you understand what's riding on this.

1149
00:42:57.040 --> 00:42:58.560
So I just finished a movie.

1150
00:42:58.560 --> 00:43:01.050
I think it's going to be out soon, I think May.

1151
00:43:01.050 --> 00:43:02.640
I'm with Michael Keaton and Sam Jackson.

1152
00:43:02.640 --> 00:43:04.840
Martin Campbell directed, you know he did Casino Royale,

1153
00:43:04.840 --> 00:43:07.800
Gold Knives, Zorro, big director.

1154
00:43:07.800 --> 00:43:11.310
And we do this, movie and there's just things.

1155
00:43:11.310 --> 00:43:15.421
And he's like, darling, no.
(Rich laughs)

1156
00:43:15.421 --> 00:43:17.070
And I'm like Martin, but Martin.

1157
00:43:17.070 --> 00:43:19.590
And so we would get into these things, you know,

1158
00:43:19.590 --> 00:43:22.400
and one of the things he didn't want me to do,

1159
00:43:22.400 --> 00:43:23.233
was this stunt.

1160
00:43:23.233 --> 00:43:25.140
I mean, there's only two stunts in my career

1161
00:43:25.140 --> 00:43:28.340
that I've actually had an amount of fear before.

1162
00:43:28.340 --> 00:43:30.200
'Cause I really don't have a lot of fear.

1163
00:43:30.200 --> 00:43:33.220
And so just done this recent movie

1164
00:43:33.220 --> 00:43:35.900
where I'm running, I'm jumping.

1165
00:43:35.900 --> 00:43:39.230
I jumped backwards off four stories,

1166
00:43:39.230 --> 00:43:41.893
and I'm taking out these guys on each level.

1167
00:43:42.760 --> 00:43:44.870
And the rehearsal process was really,

1168
00:43:44.870 --> 00:43:47.100
and Martin was just like, he was just pulling his hair out.

1169
00:43:47.100 --> 00:43:49.040
He's like, I cannot believe you're gonna do this.

1170
00:43:49.040 --> 00:43:50.273
I'm not only am I gonna do it,

1171
00:43:50.273 --> 00:43:53.100
It's gonna be one shot on this.

1172
00:43:53.100 --> 00:43:54.410
You know we're gonna arm out,

1173
00:43:54.410 --> 00:43:56.420
and it's gonna be me all the way.

1174
00:43:56.420 --> 00:43:58.280
You're gonna follow me all the way down.

1175
00:43:58.280 --> 00:43:59.560
'Cause if I'm going to risk my...

1176
00:43:59.560 --> 00:44:01.570
We need to see it, in very real way.

1177
00:44:01.570 --> 00:44:04.520
To the point where like we had a camera man

1178
00:44:04.520 --> 00:44:06.630
who actually couldn't get it on the first day.

1179
00:44:06.630 --> 00:44:08.510
I was 10 hours in a wire, he couldn't get it.

1180
00:44:08.510 --> 00:44:12.050
I had to do another day of jumping off four stories

1181
00:44:12.050 --> 00:44:13.910
because he couldn't get it.

1182
00:44:13.910 --> 00:44:14.743
Right (chuckles).

1183
00:44:14.743 --> 00:44:17.232
It was just you know-

1184
00:44:17.232 --> 00:44:20.950
Have you not been in a Tarantino movie?

1185
00:44:20.950 --> 00:44:24.080
Like I would feel like he'd be the first guy to sign you up

1186
00:44:24.080 --> 00:44:28.270
to do some crazy stunt, you know, martial arts-

1187
00:44:28.270 --> 00:44:31.170
I don't like his violence, I just don't.

1188
00:44:32.010 --> 00:44:34.530
I Mean, like I'm not saying he's not a good director,

1189
00:44:34.530 --> 00:44:35.710
like none of that, you know.

1190
00:44:35.710 --> 00:44:38.140
I mean, he's kind of, it's just not my...

1191
00:44:38.140 --> 00:44:41.380
I really dislike his violence.

1192
00:44:41.380 --> 00:44:43.929
It's just, it's so gratuitous.

1193
00:44:43.929 --> 00:44:46.160
I like fight scenes in a movie and stuff,

1194
00:44:46.160 --> 00:44:49.710
but like gratuitous and ultra gory is not my thing

1195
00:44:49.710 --> 00:44:51.450
Right.
I really-

1196
00:44:51.450 --> 00:44:56.343
I wanna know more about how you got cast in Mission,

1197
00:44:57.920 --> 00:45:01.160
from what I understand like JJ just discovered you,

1198
00:45:01.160 --> 00:45:03.060
you know found out what you were doing in Hong Kong,

1199
00:45:03.060 --> 00:45:04.230
and that's how it came together.

1200
00:45:04.230 --> 00:45:06.100
Yeah, is that funny?
Yeah.

1201
00:45:06.100 --> 00:45:08.240
Well, I had met this agent from CAA,

1202
00:45:08.240 --> 00:45:09.920
sort of six months before this happened

1203
00:45:09.920 --> 00:45:12.270
and he met me at a party and he was like, wait a minute.

1204
00:45:12.270 --> 00:45:13.560
I'm sorry, who are you?

1205
00:45:13.560 --> 00:45:15.406
What are you doing here?

1206
00:45:15.406 --> 00:45:17.030
And I said, oh, I live here, I work here.

1207
00:45:17.030 --> 00:45:17.927
And he's like, you do movies here.

1208
00:45:17.927 --> 00:45:18.760
And I'm like yeah.

1209
00:45:18.760 --> 00:45:20.458
No accent, wait you're American.

1210
00:45:20.458 --> 00:45:21.300
And he's like but you're American?

1211
00:45:21.300 --> 00:45:22.150
I'm like yeah, I'm American.

1212
00:45:22.150 --> 00:45:23.440
I just happened.

1213
00:45:23.440 --> 00:45:25.400
And he said, you'll be in Hollywood six months.

1214
00:45:25.400 --> 00:45:27.700
And I was like, he's like, does that interest you?

1215
00:45:27.700 --> 00:45:30.100
I said, not even remotely.

1216
00:45:30.100 --> 00:45:31.280
How can it not interest you.

1217
00:45:31.280 --> 00:45:33.130
What were you thinking in the back of your mind?

1218
00:45:33.130 --> 00:45:33.963
Like eventually,

1219
00:45:33.963 --> 00:45:36.513
like I'll be able to do something in the States.

1220
00:45:37.600 --> 00:45:39.170
I don't know what I was thinking.

1221
00:45:39.170 --> 00:45:42.110
I wasn't a big picture person at the time.

1222
00:45:42.110 --> 00:45:44.760
I think I was in survival mode,

1223
00:45:44.760 --> 00:45:47.320
and it was sort of like I was going to just

1224
00:45:47.320 --> 00:45:51.020
accomplish what was in front of me to the best of my ability

1225
00:45:51.020 --> 00:45:53.170
and hope that I can build from there.

1226
00:45:53.170 --> 00:45:56.370
And so I think I was very small picture at the time,

1227
00:45:56.370 --> 00:45:57.203
I have to say.

1228
00:45:57.203 --> 00:46:01.359
And then he just said, yeah you'll be in Hollywood.

1229
00:46:01.359 --> 00:46:04.300
I was like, that to me, doesn't spell success.

1230
00:46:04.300 --> 00:46:07.180
I mean, if I'm happy, and I like what I'm doing,

1231
00:46:07.180 --> 00:46:09.950
wherever that is, that's success to me.

1232
00:46:09.950 --> 00:46:12.720
And he's like, you have no idea what you're talking about.

1233
00:46:12.720 --> 00:46:15.720
So anyway, I mean six months to the month,

1234
00:46:15.720 --> 00:46:17.930
you know, I get this call.

1235
00:46:17.930 --> 00:46:18.840
I have to fly to LA.

1236
00:46:18.840 --> 00:46:23.190
And apparently like JJ had cast like 200 women.

1237
00:46:23.190 --> 00:46:25.680
I mean, I'd seen 200 women for this role.

1238
00:46:25.680 --> 00:46:28.255
And he was like, no, it's not the person yet.

1239
00:46:28.255 --> 00:46:29.490
There's someone out there.

1240
00:46:29.490 --> 00:46:34.490
So I fly from Asia here and I land that evening.

1241
00:46:34.680 --> 00:46:37.193
And the next morning I wake up, I am so sick.

1242
00:46:38.813 --> 00:46:40.493
I couldn't even stand up.

1243
00:46:41.400 --> 00:46:44.030
I had 105 degree temperature.

1244
00:46:44.030 --> 00:46:45.170
I called the casting director

1245
00:46:45.170 --> 00:46:48.680
and I said, oh my God I don't know what's happening.

1246
00:46:48.680 --> 00:46:49.513
I'm so sick.

1247
00:46:49.513 --> 00:46:51.190
And she's like, we're coming to get you.

1248
00:46:51.190 --> 00:46:52.200
We're coming against you.

1249
00:46:52.200 --> 00:46:53.610
So she comes and takes me-

1250
00:46:53.610 --> 00:46:54.450
Is that April Webster?

1251
00:46:54.450 --> 00:46:56.397
April, who's the kindest.

1252
00:46:56.397 --> 00:46:58.580
I mean, if anyone's listening and wants to be cast

1253
00:46:58.580 --> 00:46:59.730
in something like she's the one.

1254
00:46:59.730 --> 00:47:01.510
I mean, she's so kind.

1255
00:47:01.510 --> 00:47:04.290
So she came over, they got me, got me to Paramount.

1256
00:47:04.290 --> 00:47:07.270
I am so sick that I'm shaking.

1257
00:47:07.270 --> 00:47:10.960
I'm going from like sweating, like fever.

1258
00:47:10.960 --> 00:47:13.160
Like you can't even like, I wanna tear all my clothes off

1259
00:47:13.160 --> 00:47:16.820
to being so cold that I couldn't even hold a tea in my hand.

1260
00:47:16.820 --> 00:47:18.430
Like when I walked in the room, see JJ,

1261
00:47:18.430 --> 00:47:19.263
my hands were like this,

1262
00:47:19.263 --> 00:47:20.570
and the tea was spilling all over me.

1263
00:47:20.570 --> 00:47:22.830
'Cause I'd gone through a cold spell

1264
00:47:22.830 --> 00:47:26.730
and April was like Maggie, and she really helped me.

1265
00:47:26.730 --> 00:47:31.730
She said, it's 10 minutes, you're doing three scenes max.

1266
00:47:32.240 --> 00:47:34.490
You can change your life in 10 minutes.

1267
00:47:34.490 --> 00:47:37.300
And I know it's you, I just know it's you.

1268
00:47:37.300 --> 00:47:39.930
So I need you to go in there and get this movie.

1269
00:47:39.930 --> 00:47:41.650
And I was like, oh my God.

1270
00:47:41.650 --> 00:47:43.790
I mean, I was delirious.
Wow.

1271
00:47:43.790 --> 00:47:48.400
And then I did the audition and JJ on the spot said-

1272
00:47:48.400 --> 00:47:50.540
You did it in front of JJ, he was there for the audition.

1273
00:47:50.540 --> 00:47:52.440
Tom was promoting one of the world's at the time.

1274
00:47:52.440 --> 00:47:54.300
He was very involved in the casting process

1275
00:47:54.300 --> 00:47:55.133
but he couldn't be there.

1276
00:47:55.133 --> 00:47:56.470
And normally he would be there

1277
00:47:56.470 --> 00:47:59.260
once it was like kind of honed into a few people.

1278
00:47:59.260 --> 00:48:02.720
And on the spot, JJ said I will do anything

1279
00:48:02.720 --> 00:48:04.000
to get you into the (murmurs) you have to be in this movie.

1280
00:48:04.000 --> 00:48:06.010
We're doing this movie together.

1281
00:48:06.010 --> 00:48:08.940
And I was so sick that I said,

1282
00:48:08.940 --> 00:48:11.357
I think I have to go to the hospital (both laughs).

1283
00:48:12.850 --> 00:48:14.470
So I go to the hospital.

1284
00:48:14.470 --> 00:48:15.610
He knew you were sick though.

1285
00:48:15.610 --> 00:48:16.740
Oh, he knew I was sick.

1286
00:48:16.740 --> 00:48:19.200
But he also was just like, you gotta bring it

1287
00:48:19.200 --> 00:48:20.300
because it's not just me.

1288
00:48:20.300 --> 00:48:23.670
I have to please the studio heads and Tom and everyone else.

1289
00:48:23.670 --> 00:48:25.870
So I went to the hospital,

1290
00:48:25.870 --> 00:48:29.000
I woke up the next day in my room, like delirious.

1291
00:48:29.000 --> 00:48:33.670
I almost, I kind of remembered what I did, but not really.

1292
00:48:33.670 --> 00:48:38.250
Cause I was just so fevery and I had this basket in my room.

1293
00:48:38.250 --> 00:48:41.160
It was the biggest basket I've ever seen in my life.

1294
00:48:41.160 --> 00:48:42.237
I mean, it was like the size of the...

1295
00:48:42.237 --> 00:48:43.770
I mean you can't even believe it.

1296
00:48:43.770 --> 00:48:45.560
And I was like, I don't know anyone in LA,

1297
00:48:45.560 --> 00:48:47.630
why would I have a basket in my room?

1298
00:48:47.630 --> 00:48:49.690
'Cause I wasn't sure what happened.

1299
00:48:49.690 --> 00:48:52.180
And then I sort of had a card on it,

1300
00:48:52.180 --> 00:48:53.120
and I took the card off.

1301
00:48:53.120 --> 00:48:57.392
And it said here's to a great mission, love Tom and JJ.

1302
00:48:57.392 --> 00:48:58.925
And that's when it like hit me

1303
00:48:58.925 --> 00:48:59.840
that I actually got the movie.

1304
00:48:59.840 --> 00:49:01.130
It self-destruct though.

1305
00:49:01.130 --> 00:49:02.150
Yeah, it didn't blow up.
(Rich laughs)

1306
00:49:02.150 --> 00:49:04.867
Yeah, I got to eat all the crackers and figs (laughs).

1307
00:49:05.730 --> 00:49:08.410
What's funny about the way that you tell these stories

1308
00:49:08.410 --> 00:49:10.678
is you paint yourself

1309
00:49:10.678 --> 00:49:13.870
as very much like this happy-go-lucky person

1310
00:49:13.870 --> 00:49:16.800
who's kind of just bouncing around and like, oh my goodness,

1311
00:49:16.800 --> 00:49:17.633
I didn't know.

1312
00:49:17.633 --> 00:49:19.110
I'm like suddenly you're in these crazy,

1313
00:49:19.110 --> 00:49:20.940
you know situations and opportunities,

1314
00:49:20.940 --> 00:49:25.360
but that doesn't have like, part of me is like,

1315
00:49:25.360 --> 00:49:26.193
I don't buy it.

1316
00:49:26.193 --> 00:49:27.820
Like, you're-
Oh my God I hope.

1317
00:49:27.820 --> 00:49:29.470
Listen if you're-

1318
00:49:29.470 --> 00:49:30.950
Tell me if there's another side to it.

1319
00:49:30.950 --> 00:49:32.320
I don't know how you...

1320
00:49:32.320 --> 00:49:36.110
First of all, you get selected by Jackie and his team.

1321
00:49:36.110 --> 00:49:39.413
So you clearly not just survive that, you thrive in that.

1322
00:49:39.413 --> 00:49:42.190
Like you rise to the top and you become the person

1323
00:49:42.190 --> 00:49:43.400
who's the go-to.

1324
00:49:43.400 --> 00:49:46.330
Like you're identifying these opportunities

1325
00:49:46.330 --> 00:49:47.420
and making the most of them, right?

1326
00:49:47.420 --> 00:49:48.751
Well, I have to tell you,

1327
00:49:48.751 --> 00:49:50.510
at the time it didn't feel like thriving.

1328
00:49:50.510 --> 00:49:53.330
Because I may be moving up the ranks

1329
00:49:53.330 --> 00:49:57.070
and I may be earning a measure of respect from these people,

1330
00:49:57.070 --> 00:50:00.710
but they never made it feel like I was thriving.

1331
00:50:00.710 --> 00:50:04.550
Like they always made sure that you were never getting ahead

1332
00:50:04.550 --> 00:50:05.383
of yourself.

1333
00:50:05.383 --> 00:50:07.170
You knew your place.
100%.

1334
00:50:07.170 --> 00:50:08.490
So it was a real struggle.

1335
00:50:08.490 --> 00:50:11.650
And then when I got Mission and I was on the film,

1336
00:50:11.650 --> 00:50:13.920
I still felt like that person

1337
00:50:13.920 --> 00:50:15.740
who had to like earn everything,

1338
00:50:15.740 --> 00:50:17.230
in every second, in every moment

1339
00:50:17.230 --> 00:50:20.190
and then, I remember the first time I got a compliment,

1340
00:50:20.190 --> 00:50:21.070
on MI-III.
(dog barks)

1341
00:50:21.070 --> 00:50:23.616
I was like-
Oh Romeo.

1342
00:50:23.616 --> 00:50:25.870
I couldn't believe it.

1343
00:50:25.870 --> 00:50:27.727
I didn't know what was happening.

1344
00:50:27.727 --> 00:50:28.560
'Cause that doesn't happen-

1345
00:50:28.560 --> 00:50:31.116
It just didn't happen for like seven years

1346
00:50:31.116 --> 00:50:32.390
It's not part of that-
Yeah, I didn't have it.

1347
00:50:32.390 --> 00:50:33.380
And so I kind of sat back

1348
00:50:33.380 --> 00:50:36.000
and was like, what is this thing you've said to me,

1349
00:50:36.000 --> 00:50:39.200
that made me feel something inside that I shouldn't feel,

1350
00:50:39.200 --> 00:50:41.010
'cause then I'm getting ahead of myself.

1351
00:50:41.010 --> 00:50:42.260
But the minute you get to Hollywood,

1352
00:50:42.260 --> 00:50:43.660
everyone's blowing smoke up your ass.

1353
00:50:43.660 --> 00:50:46.070
Well, so that's what I mean, it's so indisingenuous.

1354
00:50:46.070 --> 00:50:48.700
So, it's sort of like, there's so many compliments

1355
00:50:48.700 --> 00:50:51.610
that go on, you know, as you know, this is Hollywood speak

1356
00:50:51.610 --> 00:50:54.950
and agents, and people I'd never experienced in my career,

1357
00:50:54.950 --> 00:50:57.470
going, oh, you're the next this, and you're that,

1358
00:50:57.470 --> 00:50:58.920
and, oh, we know you.

1359
00:50:58.920 --> 00:51:00.760
You don't know anything about me.

1360
00:51:00.760 --> 00:51:02.250
You've no idea what you're talking about.

1361
00:51:02.250 --> 00:51:04.200
Like, you don't know where I've come from.

1362
00:51:04.200 --> 00:51:07.190
Like I'm a survivor, and you're blowing sunshine up my ass

1363
00:51:07.190 --> 00:51:09.220
because you think that I'm gonna buy it.

1364
00:51:09.220 --> 00:51:10.820
But the truth is I haven't gotten a compliment

1365
00:51:10.820 --> 00:51:12.120
in eight years and I don't believe anything

1366
00:51:12.120 --> 00:51:13.270
you're saying (laughs).

1367
00:51:14.310 --> 00:51:15.850
It never affected me.

1368
00:51:15.850 --> 00:51:17.280
Like it never, people were...

1369
00:51:17.280 --> 00:51:18.530
I mean, they would say things on Mission,

1370
00:51:18.530 --> 00:51:20.300
they were just like, you're so strong,

1371
00:51:20.300 --> 00:51:22.063
and amazing, and skilled.

1372
00:51:23.390 --> 00:51:25.310
It was just this glaze.

1373
00:51:25.310 --> 00:51:28.460
I had this kinda glaze of like almost like abused child-

1374
00:51:28.460 --> 00:51:29.970
So then what was the comment that you got

1375
00:51:29.970 --> 00:51:31.820
where you actually were you're registered,

1376
00:51:31.820 --> 00:51:34.340
where you're like, oh, this is meaningful.

1377
00:51:34.340 --> 00:51:37.250
You know what, I wasn't a person who grew up

1378
00:51:37.250 --> 00:51:38.280
with a ton of confidence.

1379
00:51:38.280 --> 00:51:40.820
This is confirmed, like this I know.

1380
00:51:40.820 --> 00:51:42.430
So going into this industry,

1381
00:51:42.430 --> 00:51:45.970
I did have this work ethic that was kind of built in.

1382
00:51:45.970 --> 00:51:47.280
I have parents who worked very hard.

1383
00:51:47.280 --> 00:51:48.630
And then Jackie, right?

1384
00:51:48.630 --> 00:51:50.900
And so I'm surrounded by these people,

1385
00:51:50.900 --> 00:51:53.040
where it's like, you have to earn your way.

1386
00:51:53.040 --> 00:51:54.260
There's no free lunch here.

1387
00:51:54.260 --> 00:51:56.500
There's no like, you know, relying

1388
00:51:56.500 --> 00:52:01.060
on your God-given skill set or looks,

1389
00:52:01.060 --> 00:52:03.290
or any of this stuff, you have to work hard.

1390
00:52:03.290 --> 00:52:04.123
So, okay.

1391
00:52:04.123 --> 00:52:06.660
So I had that, and it was almost like emotional cutting.

1392
00:52:06.660 --> 00:52:08.890
It was like very punishing the way I went about things

1393
00:52:08.890 --> 00:52:12.070
and like, okay, I'm just gonna work super hard naming it.

1394
00:52:12.070 --> 00:52:16.100
But I never felt like, I had really gotten there,

1395
00:52:16.100 --> 00:52:17.430
I had earned it.

1396
00:52:17.430 --> 00:52:19.470
I was really worth much.

1397
00:52:19.470 --> 00:52:20.750
I never felt that way.

1398
00:52:20.750 --> 00:52:22.110
And that's a problem, right?

1399
00:52:22.110 --> 00:52:24.231
Because no matter what you're achieving,

1400
00:52:24.231 --> 00:52:27.830
it's never enough, but not in an obsessive way,

1401
00:52:27.830 --> 00:52:30.380
in an internal kind of sad way.

1402
00:52:30.380 --> 00:52:34.790
And so it wasn't until we were actually in Rome,

1403
00:52:34.790 --> 00:52:36.580
I think it was our first day of filming.

1404
00:52:36.580 --> 00:52:38.380
We were on the Tiber River.

1405
00:52:38.380 --> 00:52:40.510
We're speeding up and Tom-
With speed boats stuff?

1406
00:52:40.510 --> 00:52:42.400
Yeah, Tom does everything.

1407
00:52:42.400 --> 00:52:44.280
So he's manning the boat.

1408
00:52:44.280 --> 00:52:45.147
He's the whole thing.

1409
00:52:45.147 --> 00:52:47.140
And so we had a guy like kind of crouched

1410
00:52:47.140 --> 00:52:48.140
on the bottom.
(Rich laughs)

1411
00:52:48.140 --> 00:52:50.970
If we have horse, we had some like electrical failure

1412
00:52:50.970 --> 00:52:51.803
or something.

1413
00:52:51.803 --> 00:52:54.150
But he wasn't doing it, Tom was doing everything.

1414
00:52:54.150 --> 00:52:55.340
So it was me, it was the team.

1415
00:52:55.340 --> 00:52:58.200
It was Tom, myself, Ving Rhames, and Jonathan Rhys Meyers,

1416
00:52:58.200 --> 00:52:59.050
during this boat.

1417
00:53:00.020 --> 00:53:04.820
And we have, you know, they're changing lens or something.

1418
00:53:04.820 --> 00:53:07.150
So we're at our ones, and we're just sitting there

1419
00:53:07.150 --> 00:53:10.260
in this boat and it was so intimidating,

1420
00:53:10.260 --> 00:53:13.280
'cause there was maybe 5,000 people that had lined

1421
00:53:13.280 --> 00:53:14.292
just to get a glimpse of him.

1422
00:53:14.292 --> 00:53:15.125
Line up on the side of the river.

1423
00:53:15.125 --> 00:53:18.800
Oh, I mean as far as the eye could see, and you're like,

1424
00:53:18.800 --> 00:53:21.330
holy shiet, I'm standing next to a movie star.

1425
00:53:21.330 --> 00:53:23.670
This is a movie star, like legit.

1426
00:53:23.670 --> 00:53:25.810
Like there's no question, this man...

1427
00:53:25.810 --> 00:53:27.470
Like the power that he holds.

1428
00:53:27.470 --> 00:53:30.440
I mean just a glimpse of him, like they were, it was crazy.

1429
00:53:30.440 --> 00:53:31.510
So anyway, I'm sitting in this boat,

1430
00:53:31.510 --> 00:53:33.570
and it was a really intimidating day

1431
00:53:33.570 --> 00:53:35.807
although I felt sort of like, no, I felt good about it

1432
00:53:35.807 --> 00:53:37.280
and it was fine.

1433
00:53:37.280 --> 00:53:38.920
And we're sitting in the boat, and Tom's like, Maggie,

1434
00:53:38.920 --> 00:53:39.900
tell me about yourself.

1435
00:53:39.900 --> 00:53:41.750
Like, I haven't seen any of your US movies.

1436
00:53:41.750 --> 00:53:44.735
And I was like, I don't have US movies.

1437
00:53:44.735 --> 00:53:46.543
(Rich laughs)

1438
00:53:46.543 --> 00:53:48.119
He's like what?

1439
00:53:48.119 --> 00:53:51.100
And he was like, I don't understand, what do you mean?

1440
00:53:51.100 --> 00:53:55.703
And I said, oh, this is my first US movie.

1441
00:53:56.740 --> 00:53:59.070
And he goes, you're kidding me.

1442
00:53:59.070 --> 00:54:01.840
And I said no, no, this is my first US movie.

1443
00:54:01.840 --> 00:54:03.930
And he's like, I don't this, there's no way.

1444
00:54:03.930 --> 00:54:04.810
He's like Ving?

1445
00:54:04.810 --> 00:54:05.743
And Ving, he's like on his phone or something.

1446
00:54:05.743 --> 00:54:07.250
And, he's like Ving get over her.

1447
00:54:07.250 --> 00:54:08.460
And Ving is like, hey, what's going on?

1448
00:54:08.460 --> 00:54:11.534
And he goes, this is Maggie's first US movie.

1449
00:54:11.534 --> 00:54:13.484
(Rich laughs)
And Ving goes, no shiet.

1450
00:54:14.369 --> 00:54:15.210
And I'm like, yeah.

1451
00:54:15.210 --> 00:54:16.640
And he's like, damn,

1452
00:54:16.640 --> 00:54:18.390
he's like Johnny, Johnny, you believe this.

1453
00:54:18.390 --> 00:54:19.223
And he brings down (murmurs)

1454
00:54:19.223 --> 00:54:20.250
It's like so embarrassing.

1455
00:54:20.250 --> 00:54:22.210
So Johnny comes over, and he's like,

1456
00:54:22.210 --> 00:54:24.285
Johnny, this is Maggie's first US movie.

1457
00:54:24.285 --> 00:54:26.210
And Johnny is like really, no way, blah, blah.

1458
00:54:26.210 --> 00:54:28.150
So everybody's like having this conversation about me

1459
00:54:28.150 --> 00:54:29.470
in front of me.

1460
00:54:29.470 --> 00:54:31.240
And I'm like, yeah, that's it.

1461
00:54:31.240 --> 00:54:32.670
And Tom's like, let me get this straight.

1462
00:54:32.670 --> 00:54:34.630
Let me get this straight.

1463
00:54:34.630 --> 00:54:36.550
You have not done a movie in the US,

1464
00:54:36.550 --> 00:54:39.840
and then the first movie you do is like a $200 million,

1465
00:54:39.840 --> 00:54:40.820
like monstrosity,

1466
00:54:40.820 --> 00:54:43.440
where we're like on the Tiber river in Rome,

1467
00:54:43.440 --> 00:54:48.050
speeding up and down with this 200 man crew, blah, blah.

1468
00:54:48.050 --> 00:54:48.883
What was your first experience?

1469
00:54:48.883 --> 00:54:51.160
I said, yeah, that's right.

1470
00:54:51.160 --> 00:54:53.770
And he goes, you know Maggie,

1471
00:54:53.770 --> 00:54:56.510
if you didn't tell me that, he goes, I would never know it.

1472
00:54:56.510 --> 00:54:58.863
He's like, you act like you belong here.

1473
00:55:00.450 --> 00:55:03.170
And I don't know where it came from.

1474
00:55:03.170 --> 00:55:06.540
I looked at him and I said, I do belong here.

1475
00:55:06.540 --> 00:55:08.010
And he looked at me and he said,

1476
00:55:08.010 --> 00:55:09.980
you're goddamn right you do.

1477
00:55:09.980 --> 00:55:11.236
That's fucking cool.

1478
00:55:11.236 --> 00:55:12.370
(Maggie laughs)

1479
00:55:12.370 --> 00:55:13.394
Like, that's a moment.

1480
00:55:13.394 --> 00:55:14.227
It was.

1481
00:55:14.227 --> 00:55:17.304
It was really like, I can't believe I just said that to him.

1482
00:55:17.304 --> 00:55:19.311
I got chills, that's pretty cool.

1483
00:55:19.311 --> 00:55:20.870
Where did that even come from?

1484
00:55:20.870 --> 00:55:23.170
Like, I don't have the confidence to say that,

1485
00:55:23.170 --> 00:55:25.870
but I know that I put in eight year

1486
00:55:25.870 --> 00:55:28.783
of blood, sweat and tears, literally, by the way.

1487
00:55:30.080 --> 00:55:31.570
And I was there,

1488
00:55:31.570 --> 00:55:33.260
and I'm like, well, screw it,

1489
00:55:33.260 --> 00:55:35.760
like why shouldn't I be here?

1490
00:55:35.760 --> 00:55:39.840
But, that is not to say that, I took it for granted,

1491
00:55:39.840 --> 00:55:41.540
where I thought I was like special,

1492
00:55:41.540 --> 00:55:42.580
and like, oh it had to be me.

1493
00:55:42.580 --> 00:55:45.170
No, by the way, like, I don't care who it is.

1494
00:55:45.170 --> 00:55:46.850
It can always be someone else.

1495
00:55:46.850 --> 00:55:48.230
It doesn't have to be you.

1496
00:55:48.230 --> 00:55:49.110
It doesn't have to be me.

1497
00:55:49.110 --> 00:55:50.080
You know what I mean?

1498
00:55:50.080 --> 00:55:52.050
So it's keeping that in mind.

1499
00:55:52.050 --> 00:55:54.040
I think that keeps it all into perspective

1500
00:55:54.040 --> 00:55:55.210
Right.
For me in Hollywood.

1501
00:55:55.210 --> 00:55:57.150
Right.
That's such a good story.

1502
00:55:57.150 --> 00:55:57.983
It's really cool.

1503
00:55:57.983 --> 00:55:59.274
Like, I'm just trying to-

1504
00:55:59.274 --> 00:56:00.630
I don't think I've ever told that story, (laughs).

1505
00:56:00.630 --> 00:56:03.450
All the people on the side of the river,

1506
00:56:03.450 --> 00:56:05.042
and you're in the boat and the whole thing.

1507
00:56:05.042 --> 00:56:06.850
Yeah, it was a whole thing.

1508
00:56:06.850 --> 00:56:09.130
'Cause again, I don't even know where it came from.

1509
00:56:09.130 --> 00:56:12.299
Like, I didn't have what it took to say that to Tom Cruise.

1510
00:56:12.299 --> 00:56:13.940
(Maggie laughs)
Well clearly, you're right.

1511
00:56:13.940 --> 00:56:16.918
And he was right, 'cause you're still here.

1512
00:56:16.918 --> 00:56:19.206
You're still doing it.
By the grace of God (laughs)

1513
00:56:19.206 --> 00:56:23.670
So what happened with, I mean, that movie was enormous.

1514
00:56:23.670 --> 00:56:25.683
But there were all these other mission movies,

1515
00:56:25.683 --> 00:56:27.170
that came after that, right?

1516
00:56:27.170 --> 00:56:29.620
Like what, there was some cast changes,

1517
00:56:29.620 --> 00:56:31.860
and how didn't you end up in, you know all of them?

1518
00:56:31.860 --> 00:56:34.967
