01:05:00.490 --> 01:05:03.100
And you need the person who can work within McDonald's

1771
01:05:03.100 --> 01:05:05.480
to create change from inside.

1772
01:05:05.480 --> 01:05:09.550
I mean, I work with a group, I'm on the board

1773
01:05:09.550 --> 01:05:11.840
of a group called Social Compassion and Legislation.

1774
01:05:11.840 --> 01:05:14.410
We do a lot of legislative work up in Sacramento,

1775
01:05:14.410 --> 01:05:18.087
and you know, it is the epitome of that.

1776
01:05:18.087 --> 01:05:20.780
So you're sort of like, you know, you're going

1777
01:05:20.780 --> 01:05:23.640
into these meetings with these senators, and assembly men,

1778
01:05:23.640 --> 01:05:26.020
and people who can, you know, these are lawmakers.

1779
01:05:26.020 --> 01:05:30.350
These are people that really essentially work for us, right?

1780
01:05:30.350 --> 01:05:33.530
And you know, I go there, and I'm sort of lobbying senators

1781
01:05:33.530 --> 01:05:35.923
and you know (laughs) in this building

1782
01:05:35.923 --> 01:05:39.830
and then there's no one there, and I'm driving down Melrose

1783
01:05:39.830 --> 01:05:44.140
and there's 40 people in line for lip gloss.

1784
01:05:44.140 --> 01:05:45.540
And it bums me out,

1785
01:05:45.540 --> 01:05:47.600
because it's like we have so much influence,

1786
01:05:47.600 --> 01:05:48.950
all you have to do is care.

1787
01:05:48.950 --> 01:05:49.870
All you have to do is show up.

1788
01:05:49.870 --> 01:05:51.050
Half of it showing up, right?

1789
01:05:51.050 --> 01:05:52.260
Life gotta show up.

1790
01:05:52.260 --> 01:05:53.780
And then once you show up,

1791
01:05:53.780 --> 01:05:55.880
you really have to like be in those rooms,

1792
01:05:55.880 --> 01:05:58.160
with people that may not get it.

1793
01:05:58.160 --> 01:06:00.360
But what you're gonna do in those rooms,

1794
01:06:00.360 --> 01:06:02.250
can be pretty remarkable.

1795
01:06:02.250 --> 01:06:06.710
Well, it's one thing to be a proponent of this lifestyle.

1796
01:06:06.710 --> 01:06:10.100
And it's another thing to really shoulder that mantle,

1797
01:06:10.100 --> 01:06:11.820
and carry that responsibility

1798
01:06:11.820 --> 01:06:15.861
to use like the platform that you have to advocate,

1799
01:06:15.861 --> 01:06:17.740
on behalf of these causes.

1800
01:06:17.740 --> 01:06:20.700
So where does that come from in you?

1801
01:06:20.700 --> 01:06:21.580
Cause it would be very easy

1802
01:06:21.580 --> 01:06:24.320
for you to be like, I'm just, I'm doing my movies.

1803
01:06:24.320 --> 01:06:25.560
I don't wanna make waves.

1804
01:06:25.560 --> 01:06:27.705
Sure, it is much easier to do that.

1805
01:06:27.705 --> 01:06:29.724
I don't wanna upset people.
Yeah-

1806
01:06:29.724 --> 01:06:32.553
So where does that pull come from?

1807
01:06:33.980 --> 01:06:35.843
I kind of feel like,

1808
01:06:38.366 --> 01:06:41.347
it's almost not even a choice in that.

1809
01:06:41.347 --> 01:06:45.000
You know, we live this very privileged existence,

1810
01:06:45.000 --> 01:06:46.560
like in every way.

1811
01:06:46.560 --> 01:06:50.030
And I mean that in things that I've earned,

1812
01:06:50.030 --> 01:06:51.460
I mean it in things that I'm living,

1813
01:06:51.460 --> 01:06:52.730
like okay, I'm given my health,

1814
01:06:52.730 --> 01:06:55.890
I have this gift of health and I can walk and I function.

1815
01:06:55.890 --> 01:06:56.830
So that's a gift.

1816
01:06:56.830 --> 01:06:58.520
And then I've earned these other things,

1817
01:06:58.520 --> 01:07:01.350
where I work in Hollywood, and I have certain privileges,

1818
01:07:01.350 --> 01:07:04.760
and you know, you start to develop a voice

1819
01:07:04.760 --> 01:07:08.370
for certain things, and it doesn't feel like a choice.

1820
01:07:08.370 --> 01:07:10.223
It feels like a responsibility.

1821
01:07:11.390 --> 01:07:15.590
When you have a lot, how do you not...

1822
01:07:15.590 --> 01:07:17.713
And it can be anything, you know, pick what it is

1823
01:07:17.713 --> 01:07:22.580
that you sort of feel isn't right in your mind,

1824
01:07:22.580 --> 01:07:24.020
in your heart, in your soul.

1825
01:07:24.020 --> 01:07:26.700
And you go out there, and you really, you fight for it.

1826
01:07:26.700 --> 01:07:28.440
And you hope that other people will do the same,

1827
01:07:28.440 --> 01:07:29.560
when something matters to them,

1828
01:07:29.560 --> 01:07:30.840
because I'm sure you get this all the time.

1829
01:07:30.840 --> 01:07:32.220
I've gotten it for 20 years.

1830
01:07:32.220 --> 01:07:33.563
Like, oh, you don't care about kids.

1831
01:07:33.563 --> 01:07:35.010
You don't care about women.

1832
01:07:35.010 --> 01:07:37.653
You don't care about libraries, I don't know.

1833
01:07:37.653 --> 01:07:40.469
Because you've chosen to advocate for one thing.

1834
01:07:40.469 --> 01:07:44.090
That's at the exclusion of other things that are important.

1835
01:07:44.090 --> 01:07:44.923
This is exactly it.

1836
01:07:44.923 --> 01:07:47.180
And like, you're so right, I hate children,

1837
01:07:47.180 --> 01:07:49.760
because I love the environment or whatever it is, you know.

1838
01:07:49.760 --> 01:07:51.530
And it sort of is there's always this line,

1839
01:07:51.530 --> 01:07:53.870
and so it's always this thing of like,

1840
01:07:53.870 --> 01:07:56.040
I have people that write into me and go,

1841
01:07:56.040 --> 01:07:57.700
you care more about homeless pets,

1842
01:07:57.700 --> 01:07:59.190
than you do about homeless children.

1843
01:07:59.190 --> 01:08:00.600
I'm like interesting.

1844
01:08:00.600 --> 01:08:02.830
And I said, I'm so glad that you care

1845
01:08:02.830 --> 01:08:04.440
about homeless children.

1846
01:08:04.440 --> 01:08:05.400
Well, I do.

1847
01:08:05.400 --> 01:08:06.910
I said, well, tell me more.

1848
01:08:06.910 --> 01:08:08.310
What do you do for homeless children?

1849
01:08:08.310 --> 01:08:09.760
I'm fascinated, I wanna know.

1850
01:08:10.960 --> 01:08:13.520
Nothing, absolutely nothing.

1851
01:08:13.520 --> 01:08:15.950
So I've never, ever, run into a person

1852
01:08:15.950 --> 01:08:17.310
who puts themselves out there,

1853
01:08:17.310 --> 01:08:19.610
who advocates for something they care about

1854
01:08:19.610 --> 01:08:23.350
regardless of what it is, who has ever criticized me.

1855
01:08:23.350 --> 01:08:26.090
You know, when I'm in rooms with women's rights activists,

1856
01:08:26.090 --> 01:08:28.400
my human rights friends in DC,

1857
01:08:28.400 --> 01:08:30.130
we all kind of look at each other

1858
01:08:30.130 --> 01:08:31.680
and go thank you for what you do,

1859
01:08:31.680 --> 01:08:33.260
because what you do matters.

1860
01:08:33.260 --> 01:08:35.520
In your lane, and in your category.

1861
01:08:35.520 --> 01:08:36.730
It's always people who do nothing,

1862
01:08:36.730 --> 01:08:39.430
who have a ton to say, about what you're doing.

1863
01:08:39.430 --> 01:08:41.892
How often have you gone to Washington,

1864
01:08:41.892 --> 01:08:42.725
and done the health thing.

1865
01:08:42.725 --> 01:08:44.680
One, god I'm set to go this year too.

1866
01:08:44.680 --> 01:08:46.150
I just got a phone call yesterday,

1867
01:08:46.150 --> 01:08:50.230
because we're really on the match

1868
01:08:51.460 --> 01:08:53.180
for more federal funding

1869
01:08:53.180 --> 01:08:55.360
for some of the child protection stuff that I do.

1870
01:08:55.360 --> 01:08:59.780
And it's really daunting

1871
01:08:59.780 --> 01:09:01.840
when you look at sort of budgets,

1872
01:09:01.840 --> 01:09:06.440
and you know what are policymakers, and lawmakers, you know

1873
01:09:06.440 --> 01:09:09.420
allocate for certain things and not for others.

1874
01:09:09.420 --> 01:09:12.800
And I sort of went down this rabbit hole many years ago

1875
01:09:12.800 --> 01:09:14.770
where it was like my birthday weekend.

1876
01:09:14.770 --> 01:09:16.980
And there was this child abuse prevention summit

1877
01:09:16.980 --> 01:09:18.489
that I went to in San Diego.

1878
01:09:18.489 --> 01:09:21.360
And I was there for the weekend,

1879
01:09:21.360 --> 01:09:23.980
and the Rabbit Hole for me was huge,

1880
01:09:23.980 --> 01:09:24.880
because everyone was there,

1881
01:09:24.880 --> 01:09:27.260
everyone from the CDC, to child protective services,

1882
01:09:27.260 --> 01:09:29.700
to forensic physicians, to law enforcement,

1883
01:09:29.700 --> 01:09:30.820
everyone was there.

1884
01:09:30.820 --> 01:09:32.500
So it was this think tank,

1885
01:09:32.500 --> 01:09:35.010
of how do we better protect children?

1886
01:09:35.010 --> 01:09:37.460
And the CDC had done this presentation.

1887
01:09:37.460 --> 01:09:40.320
And to be very honest, it was really quite boring.

1888
01:09:40.320 --> 01:09:44.530
And then towards the end, she busted out this sort of graph.

1889
01:09:44.530 --> 01:09:46.500
And it was like almost this sputnik kind of chart,

1890
01:09:46.500 --> 01:09:49.570
where at the center was abuse and neglect.

1891
01:09:49.570 --> 01:09:52.083
And then everything that came from that,

1892
01:09:52.083 --> 01:09:56.517
sort of armed off into all these different societal issues.

1893
01:09:56.517 --> 01:09:59.690
And I remember like that was like the moment

1894
01:09:59.690 --> 01:10:01.950
where it just dropped for me,

1895
01:10:01.950 --> 01:10:05.040
where I was looking at everything from suicide,

1896
01:10:05.040 --> 01:10:07.690
opiate addiction, to alcohol, to teen pregnancy,

1897
01:10:07.690 --> 01:10:09.942
to high school dropouts.

1898
01:10:09.942 --> 01:10:12.260
Everything that you can think of,

1899
01:10:12.260 --> 01:10:15.340
like in the 80th percentile was stemming from-

1900
01:10:15.340 --> 01:10:17.270
All tracks back to abuse in the home.

1901
01:10:17.270 --> 01:10:19.410
Right, from when in your formative years,

1902
01:10:19.410 --> 01:10:21.580
when you should be forming in the right way,

1903
01:10:21.580 --> 01:10:23.130
and you know, you're being betrayed,

1904
01:10:23.130 --> 01:10:24.250
and take advantage of.

1905
01:10:24.250 --> 01:10:25.500
And so...

1906
01:10:26.950 --> 01:10:27.820
I mean that was it for me.

1907
01:10:27.820 --> 01:10:30.500
It was just sort of like I had read a couple things

1908
01:10:30.500 --> 01:10:33.030
in the last LA times over the years.

1909
01:10:33.030 --> 01:10:34.350
I remember eight years prior,

1910
01:10:34.350 --> 01:10:35.870
I had read this story about this kid

1911
01:10:35.870 --> 01:10:40.870
who was like tied to a chair by his mom and boyfriend,

1912
01:10:41.610 --> 01:10:42.443
and he was beaten to death.

1913
01:10:42.443 --> 01:10:43.760
He was six.

1914
01:10:43.760 --> 01:10:46.310
And they had a file on him,

1915
01:10:46.310 --> 01:10:48.257
you know the child protective services,

1916
01:10:48.257 --> 01:10:50.500
they were under investigation.

1917
01:10:50.500 --> 01:10:52.050
But we were failing here.

1918
01:10:52.050 --> 01:10:54.780
We're failing, and then eight years later,

1919
01:10:54.780 --> 01:10:56.900
I read another story that was very similar

1920
01:10:56.900 --> 01:10:59.260
with a mom and the boyfriend, who had killed this kid.

1921
01:10:59.260 --> 01:11:00.260
He was like eight.

1922
01:11:00.260 --> 01:11:02.410
And the second time I had read about it,

1923
01:11:02.410 --> 01:11:04.190
like that fury in me,

1924
01:11:04.190 --> 01:11:05.830
like the same thing I have for the animals,

1925
01:11:05.830 --> 01:11:07.990
and all that sort of stuff, and the environment,

1926
01:11:07.990 --> 01:11:09.490
I couldn't ignore it anymore.

1927
01:11:09.490 --> 01:11:12.460
'Cause it was something I think it was very...

1928
01:11:12.460 --> 01:11:13.970
It just felt so personal,

1929
01:11:13.970 --> 01:11:16.300
and I was so angry that we were failing kids.

1930
01:11:16.300 --> 01:11:18.240
And these are the kids by the way that grow up

1931
01:11:18.240 --> 01:11:21.710
to abuse their partners, and animals, and all the rest of it

1932
01:11:21.710 --> 01:11:24.640
and not care because they've been so disenfranchised,

1933
01:11:24.640 --> 01:11:26.300
and they're in so much pain,

1934
01:11:26.300 --> 01:11:27.820
that there's nothing that they can care about

1935
01:11:27.820 --> 01:11:29.590
outside of their own pain.

1936
01:11:29.590 --> 01:11:32.650
And again, this is stemming from the very, very early years.

1937
01:11:32.650 --> 01:11:34.410
So I'm like if I'm gonna make a difference

1938
01:11:34.410 --> 01:11:35.990
in some of the stuff I'm doing,

1939
01:11:35.990 --> 01:11:38.960
like we talked about earlier about getting them young,

1940
01:11:38.960 --> 01:11:41.950
we really have to do everything we can do to protect them

1941
01:11:41.950 --> 01:11:42.900
at this young age.

1942
01:11:42.900 --> 01:11:44.660
And that means exploitation.

1943
01:11:44.660 --> 01:11:46.415
It means all the trafficking, abduction,

1944
01:11:46.415 --> 01:11:48.380
abuse in the home, all of it.

1945
01:11:48.380 --> 01:11:51.970
And so I did, I got involved about four, five years ago

1946
01:11:51.970 --> 01:11:54.070
and I have not stopped since.

1947
01:11:54.070 --> 01:11:56.600
And so this year we're going into DC,

1948
01:11:56.600 --> 01:11:59.020
and we're really, we've got to get more money

1949
01:11:59.020 --> 01:12:00.750
from the federal government for these programs,

1950
01:12:00.750 --> 01:12:02.500
because it's really the technology

1951
01:12:02.500 --> 01:12:03.400
that's gonna protect this kids

1952
01:12:03.400 --> 01:12:05.520
So what is the solution,

1953
01:12:05.520 --> 01:12:06.860
like where do you direct those funds,

1954
01:12:06.860 --> 01:12:08.450
or what are the policy changes,

1955
01:12:08.450 --> 01:12:10.110
that can really move the needle?

1956
01:12:10.110 --> 01:12:11.540
Policy is tough, right?

1957
01:12:11.540 --> 01:12:13.950
Because you know, if you depend on the federal government,

1958
01:12:13.950 --> 01:12:15.050
to do what you need them to do,

1959
01:12:15.050 --> 01:12:16.810
you're gonna be waiting a very long time, right? (chuckles).

1960
01:12:16.810 --> 01:12:20.990
So I work with a group of former police chiefs

1961
01:12:20.990 --> 01:12:25.410
federal agents, who have created this group

1962
01:12:25.410 --> 01:12:28.150
called the I catch cops as the internet crimes

1963
01:12:28.150 --> 01:12:30.490
against children, child online protective system.

1964
01:12:30.490 --> 01:12:33.950
And this is a system that actually finds predators online.

1965
01:12:33.950 --> 01:12:35.290
And so a lot of the money

1966
01:12:35.290 --> 01:12:37.500
really goes to upping the technology.

1967
01:12:37.500 --> 01:12:40.120
Because if you're talking about criminal activity,

1968
01:12:40.120 --> 01:12:42.280
they're good at what they do.

1969
01:12:42.280 --> 01:12:44.230
Unfortunately they know what they're doing

1970
01:12:44.230 --> 01:12:47.720
and they're trying to figure out how you're detecting them,

1971
01:12:47.720 --> 01:12:49.690
and they're trying to evade you at all costs,

1972
01:12:49.690 --> 01:12:50.700
because this is something

1973
01:12:50.700 --> 01:12:52.470
that they are absolutely addicted to.

1974
01:12:52.470 --> 01:12:56.390
And so you have to stay ahead of them, and that takes money.

1975
01:12:56.390 --> 01:12:58.958
And it takes technology, and it takes manpower.

1976
01:12:58.958 --> 01:13:03.670
So, you know, it's yeah, DC this year...

1977
01:13:03.670 --> 01:13:05.601
Yeah, that's dark though.

1978
01:13:05.601 --> 01:13:08.010
It's dark and it's something people don't take on.

1979
01:13:08.010 --> 01:13:10.670
Yeah, you have to create an emotional boundary

1980
01:13:10.670 --> 01:13:11.720
around yourself too.

1981
01:13:11.720 --> 01:13:15.810
I would imagine also just be able to, you know, deal.

1982
01:13:15.810 --> 01:13:19.930
I'll tell you that this particular area

1983
01:13:19.930 --> 01:13:22.260
of protection that I work in,

1984
01:13:22.260 --> 01:13:24.913
is the hardest thing I've ever done in my life.

1985
01:13:25.785 --> 01:13:29.390
I'll jump off a building, I'll do whatever it is.

1986
01:13:29.390 --> 01:13:32.420
You know, like making Earthlings with Shaun,

1987
01:13:32.420 --> 01:13:33.800
and seeing what I saw,

1988
01:13:33.800 --> 01:13:36.890
and what humanity has done to animals at that time.

1989
01:13:36.890 --> 01:13:41.120
And then now seeing what humanity does to each other.

1990
01:13:41.120 --> 01:13:43.870
Those are the two darkest times I think for me.

1991
01:13:43.870 --> 01:13:45.730
Darkest stuff I've ever seen in my life.

1992
01:13:45.730 --> 01:13:48.310
And the reality is it's happening.

1993
01:13:48.310 --> 01:13:52.350
And this is not a subject celebrities are gonna take on,

1994
01:13:52.350 --> 01:13:53.387
it's too dark.

1995
01:13:53.387 --> 01:13:55.460
And it's actually not something I've ever talked about.

1996
01:13:55.460 --> 01:13:56.920
Something I've done very quietly.

1997
01:13:56.920 --> 01:13:57.753
For a very long time.

1998
01:13:57.753 --> 01:13:59.339
Yeah, cause I haven't heard you talk about this

1999
01:13:59.339 --> 01:14:00.736
that much, I mean it's at all about,

2000
01:14:00.736 --> 01:14:03.130
plenty on the animal rights stuff.

2001
01:14:03.130 --> 01:14:04.070
Plenty on the (murmurs).

2002
01:14:04.070 --> 01:14:06.140
For me, it's defenseless, right?

2003
01:14:06.140 --> 01:14:07.313
It's defenseless lives.

2004
01:14:07.313 --> 01:14:11.309
Yeah, it's the same theme.
It really is the same theme.

2005
01:14:11.309 --> 01:14:12.925
Protecting people that can't protect themselves.

2006
01:14:12.925 --> 01:14:15.410
This is what it is you know,
Yeah, exactly.

2007
01:14:15.410 --> 01:14:17.510
It's, I don't know,

2008
01:14:17.510 --> 01:14:19.170
I think like going back to what you said.

2009
01:14:19.170 --> 01:14:21.730
It is a social responsibility,

2010
01:14:21.730 --> 01:14:23.080
and if you have any kind of voice,

2011
01:14:23.080 --> 01:14:24.110
I mean, look at what you've done,

2012
01:14:24.110 --> 01:14:26.780
my God, if you have any kind of voice.

2013
01:14:26.780 --> 01:14:27.670
You can truly...

2014
01:14:27.670 --> 01:14:30.160
If it's authentic, you can really turn it

2015
01:14:30.160 --> 01:14:32.500
into something very special, I do believe that.

2016
01:14:32.500 --> 01:14:35.740
So when someone comes to you and says,

2017
01:14:35.740 --> 01:14:37.500
you know, I have so much respect for what you're doing

2018
01:14:37.500 --> 01:14:40.320
or it's so courageous, but you know, you have this platform,

2019
01:14:40.320 --> 01:14:41.570
I don't have that.

2020
01:14:41.570 --> 01:14:43.270
Like how can I get involved,

2021
01:14:43.270 --> 01:14:46.640
or how do I make my voice resonate more broadly?

2022
01:14:46.640 --> 01:14:47.473
Sure.

2023
01:14:47.473 --> 01:14:50.750
Well, here's the thing, you have to believe number one,

2024
01:14:50.750 --> 01:14:52.320
because there are celebrities,

2025
01:14:52.320 --> 01:14:53.770
