01:44:37.970 --> 01:44:40.070
until the universe has your attention.

2782
01:44:40.070 --> 01:44:41.070
Until you've learned that lesson.

2783
01:44:41.070 --> 01:44:43.827
There's a philosopher, his name's John Demartini,

2784
01:44:43.827 --> 01:44:47.140
and he says, whatever we run away from, we run into.

2785
01:44:47.140 --> 01:44:47.973
Right.

2786
01:44:47.973 --> 01:44:48.806
So there's really no...

2787
01:44:48.806 --> 01:44:51.130
I mean you've got to solve it at some point, right?

2788
01:44:51.130 --> 01:44:53.280
And solving it is you.
Right.

2789
01:44:53.280 --> 01:44:54.710
It's always you.

2790
01:44:54.710 --> 01:44:55.930
But here's the thing about energy,

2791
01:44:55.930 --> 01:44:57.750
that's exciting about this.

2792
01:44:57.750 --> 01:44:59.513
As hard as it is to hear the things

2793
01:44:59.513 --> 01:45:00.810
that you don't wanna hear,

2794
01:45:00.810 --> 01:45:02.770
and make the changes you wanna make.

2795
01:45:02.770 --> 01:45:05.670
If you're always focused on yourself

2796
01:45:05.670 --> 01:45:09.650
you don't have to do anything to see the changes

2797
01:45:09.650 --> 01:45:12.060
in the person or the situation around you.

2798
01:45:12.060 --> 01:45:14.500
It will happen by virtue of you changing.

2799
01:45:14.500 --> 01:45:15.333
Right.

2800
01:45:15.333 --> 01:45:16.557
That's a universal truth.

2801
01:45:16.557 --> 01:45:17.600
That's a spiritual truth.
100%

2802
01:45:17.600 --> 01:45:18.700
It's a spiritual truth.

2803
01:45:18.700 --> 01:45:20.440
And it is a game changer.

2804
01:45:20.440 --> 01:45:25.020
And it is full-proof, there's no way you change your energy.

2805
01:45:25.020 --> 01:45:28.930
And you say to yourself, I've really got to fix this problem

2806
01:45:28.930 --> 01:45:31.940
in me and that around you, the energy doesn't change.

2807
01:45:31.940 --> 01:45:33.040
Yeah.
Impossible.

2808
01:45:33.040 --> 01:45:35.680
The problem is most people are externally focused

2809
01:45:35.680 --> 01:45:38.790
and they think, well, if I just trade up on my relationship

2810
01:45:38.790 --> 01:45:41.220
to this other person, that's gonna solve the problem.

2811
01:45:41.220 --> 01:45:46.210
But that's tantamount to just keeping the blinders on.

2812
01:45:46.210 --> 01:45:49.340
And you know, it's a mechanism to avoid having to look

2813
01:45:49.340 --> 01:45:50.560
at yourself in that way.

2814
01:45:50.560 --> 01:45:51.393
Well, that is what it is.

2815
01:45:51.393 --> 01:45:54.296
Cause what is looking at ourself, it's painful.

2816
01:45:54.296 --> 01:45:55.318
No one must be in pain.

2817
01:45:55.318 --> 01:45:56.310
No, it's the worst.

2818
01:45:56.310 --> 01:45:57.528
It's the worst, but guess what-

2819
01:45:57.528 --> 01:45:58.755
But the pain is what gets you to do it

2820
01:45:58.755 --> 01:46:00.451
But here is the thing we're always in pain.

2821
01:46:00.451 --> 01:46:01.650
(Rich laughs)
So it doesn't matter.

2822
01:46:01.650 --> 01:46:03.680
It's a sort of like, you can either put the bandaid on,

2823
01:46:03.680 --> 01:46:06.100
or you can go deep, and you can have many years

2824
01:46:06.100 --> 01:46:08.730
where you're in a lot less pain than you are now.

2825
01:46:08.730 --> 01:46:09.790
Yeah.
If you focus-

2826
01:46:09.790 --> 01:46:12.120
Was there something that like,

2827
01:46:12.120 --> 01:46:14.070
was this just a slow evolution for you?

2828
01:46:14.070 --> 01:46:17.380
Or did something happen, that made you do a little bit

2829
01:46:17.380 --> 01:46:19.856
more internal work than you would have preferred?

2830
01:46:19.856 --> 01:46:21.355
I think it was,

2831
01:46:21.355 --> 01:46:23.180
well number one, it was definitely a slow evolution.

2832
01:46:23.180 --> 01:46:25.400
Because it was like book after book, after book,

2833
01:46:25.400 --> 01:46:28.050
after you know, talk about a journey.

2834
01:46:28.050 --> 01:46:29.580
I mean, you really have to journey,

2835
01:46:29.580 --> 01:46:32.620
and take what it is that you learn and apply it.

2836
01:46:32.620 --> 01:46:34.840
So it's not just about like being a bookworm,

2837
01:46:34.840 --> 01:46:36.170
or being intelligent.

2838
01:46:36.170 --> 01:46:39.180
You have to have an IQ high enough to absorb

2839
01:46:39.180 --> 01:46:41.980
what it is that you're doing and being able to assimilate it

2840
01:46:41.980 --> 01:46:44.540
into your life, and then enter your actions.

2841
01:46:44.540 --> 01:46:48.260
But I think that as a young person and then going out there

2842
01:46:48.260 --> 01:46:49.340
in the world as a teenager

2843
01:46:49.340 --> 01:46:51.843
and having like sort to make it on my own,

2844
01:46:52.880 --> 01:46:56.740
there was a lot of pain, I think that I carried

2845
01:46:56.740 --> 01:47:00.690
and a lot of forgiveness that had to go on in my life.

2846
01:47:00.690 --> 01:47:05.690
And part of that journey to forgiving the people in my life

2847
01:47:06.100 --> 01:47:11.003
that I felt I needed to forgive, was understanding them.

2848
01:47:11.920 --> 01:47:13.380
And that was really it for me

2849
01:47:13.380 --> 01:47:15.480
when I realized that...

2850
01:47:15.480 --> 01:47:17.470
And I really don't know what did it,

2851
01:47:17.470 --> 01:47:21.157
but I went well, if I can't have a perspective

2852
01:47:21.157 --> 01:47:26.157
on the why of who they've been to me in my life,

2853
01:47:26.310 --> 01:47:28.920
then I'm never going to be able to forgive them

2854
01:47:28.920 --> 01:47:29.753
with a whole heart.

2855
01:47:29.753 --> 01:47:31.650
Because without understanding

2856
01:47:31.650 --> 01:47:33.496
how are you going to forgive?

2857
01:47:33.496 --> 01:47:35.700
Because then it's a surface, it's a bandaid.

2858
01:47:35.700 --> 01:47:36.840
It's a, yeah I forgive you,

2859
01:47:36.840 --> 01:47:39.120
cause I wanna feel good in this moment.

2860
01:47:39.120 --> 01:47:41.460
But if I really understand where you came from

2861
01:47:41.460 --> 01:47:43.760
and knowing that you had no choice in it, not that you...

2862
01:47:43.760 --> 01:47:46.070
But we know that life is hard.

2863
01:47:46.070 --> 01:47:48.584
We know that being in the body is difficult.

2864
01:47:48.584 --> 01:47:51.590
And being in the mind is even more difficult.

2865
01:47:51.590 --> 01:47:56.160
And so if you can really, you know look at the pattern

2866
01:47:56.160 --> 01:47:56.993
of someone's life

2867
01:47:56.993 --> 01:48:00.680
and say, well, they got to this point with no tools.

2868
01:48:00.680 --> 01:48:02.200
And then without those tools,

2869
01:48:02.200 --> 01:48:04.600
outwardly express themselves the way they did

2870
01:48:04.600 --> 01:48:06.400
because there was just nothing.

2871
01:48:06.400 --> 01:48:09.730
You know it's like having all like the sheet rock,

2872
01:48:09.730 --> 01:48:11.290
and that this, and the wood and everything.

2873
01:48:11.290 --> 01:48:13.930
And you're like, I'm ready to build my house.

2874
01:48:13.930 --> 01:48:15.840
And there's not a nail in sight.

2875
01:48:15.840 --> 01:48:17.210
There's not a hammer in sight.

2876
01:48:17.210 --> 01:48:20.300
Like nothing's gonna happen and you're rained on.

2877
01:48:20.300 --> 01:48:23.830
So, you know if you can recognize

2878
01:48:23.830 --> 01:48:26.650
that people don't have the tools,

2879
01:48:26.650 --> 01:48:30.980
it takes a lot of stress off of taking things personally.

2880
01:48:30.980 --> 01:48:35.330
Right, but forgiveness is tough because it requires you

2881
01:48:35.330 --> 01:48:38.820
like there's for a lot of people,

2882
01:48:38.820 --> 01:48:42.180
identity is built on this resentment that you hold

2883
01:48:42.180 --> 01:48:43.970
towards this how this person

2884
01:48:43.970 --> 01:48:46.820
or family member wronged you in a certain way.

2885
01:48:46.820 --> 01:48:48.210
And it's scary to let go

2886
01:48:48.210 --> 01:48:50.200
of that because what would that mean?

2887
01:48:50.200 --> 01:48:53.390
Like then suddenly I have to take responsibility for this

2888
01:48:53.390 --> 01:48:57.190
or if I forgive them, yes maybe I'll feel better,

2889
01:48:57.190 --> 01:49:02.190
but this whole construct upon which I've kind of crafted

2890
01:49:02.270 --> 01:49:06.220
how I see the world and myself crumbles.

2891
01:49:06.220 --> 01:49:07.053
Well, that's what it is

2892
01:49:07.053 --> 01:49:09.283
because you don't get to be a victim anymore.

2893
01:49:10.820 --> 01:49:13.470
Being a victim is a really safe place to be

2894
01:49:13.470 --> 01:49:15.060
because there's always an excuse

2895
01:49:15.060 --> 01:49:16.250
for why things aren't working out-

2896
01:49:16.250 --> 01:49:18.086
But there was a dopamine hit with it.

2897
01:49:18.086 --> 01:49:21.824
It can be very intoxicating to like indulge in that.

2898
01:49:21.824 --> 01:49:22.820
Indulge in that.

2899
01:49:22.820 --> 01:49:23.950
And it is, and people do it.

2900
01:49:23.950 --> 01:49:25.460
And that's why they turn to alcohol and drugs,

2901
01:49:25.460 --> 01:49:26.293
the way that they do.

2902
01:49:26.293 --> 01:49:28.110
But I think one thing that you just said

2903
01:49:28.110 --> 01:49:30.390
that's really important is that,

2904
01:49:30.390 --> 01:49:34.653
I think that people view forgiveness as,

2905
01:49:36.150 --> 01:49:38.970
letting someone get away with what they did.

2906
01:49:38.970 --> 01:49:42.780
Like it means, if I forgive you, it's okay what you did.

2907
01:49:42.780 --> 01:49:44.680
It's not even remotely true.

2908
01:49:44.680 --> 01:49:48.380
Forgiveness is your own personal freedom.

2909
01:49:48.380 --> 01:49:49.620
And that's all it is.

2910
01:49:49.620 --> 01:49:52.530
You no longer are held by this act or this person

2911
01:49:52.530 --> 01:49:53.520
because the truth is,

2912
01:49:53.520 --> 01:49:56.070
the act whatever it was they did to you is over, right?

2913
01:49:56.070 --> 01:49:58.100
It's never gonna happen again because it's done.

2914
01:49:58.100 --> 01:50:00.580
The only thing you take with you is the emotion.

2915
01:50:00.580 --> 01:50:03.070
So you're carrying that emotion with you, your entire life.

2916
01:50:03.070 --> 01:50:04.900
And then there's the point where you go,

2917
01:50:04.900 --> 01:50:06.650
I have to let go of this emotion,

2918
01:50:06.650 --> 01:50:08.798
because I need my freedom back, right?

2919
01:50:08.798 --> 01:50:10.380
Right, I mean, you're the one who's suffering,

2920
01:50:10.380 --> 01:50:12.610
that other person may be completely unaware.

2921
01:50:12.610 --> 01:50:13.667
They may not even know.
Yeah,

2922
01:50:13.667 --> 01:50:16.821
so basically you're punishing yourself.

2923
01:50:16.821 --> 01:50:18.520
You're punishing yourself your entire life.

2924
01:50:18.520 --> 01:50:21.660
So do you want your personal freedom?

2925
01:50:21.660 --> 01:50:23.330
Can you have faith in the process

2926
01:50:23.330 --> 01:50:26.412
that if you forgive someone, and you have that freedom,

2927
01:50:26.412 --> 01:50:31.412
you're going to gain the thing that you couldn't see.

2928
01:50:31.470 --> 01:50:33.490
You know, that which you have a belief in,

2929
01:50:33.490 --> 01:50:35.270
that you never thought was possible.

2930
01:50:35.270 --> 01:50:38.290
It's only possible once you truly forgive.

2931
01:50:38.290 --> 01:50:40.470
I'm a big advocate for forgiveness.

2932
01:50:40.470 --> 01:50:43.900
I think it is the most healing emotion you can have.

2933
01:50:43.900 --> 01:50:46.117
And the only emotion that's light enough to live with.

2934
01:50:46.117 --> 01:50:47.930
(laughs)

2935
01:50:47.930 --> 01:50:48.763
Well, look at you.

2936
01:50:48.763 --> 01:50:51.316
You could be a therapist, I'mma like sign up right now.

2937
01:50:51.316 --> 01:50:53.342
(both laugh)

2938
01:50:53.342 --> 01:50:55.020
If this acting thing doesn't work out,

2939
01:50:55.020 --> 01:50:56.690
you know Tom cruise, whatever.

2940
01:50:56.690 --> 01:50:59.973
Go into like forgiveness advocacy full time, full time.

2941
01:51:01.140 --> 01:51:02.690
Yeah, it's a journey, isn't it?

2942
01:51:02.690 --> 01:51:03.585
Right?

2943
01:51:03.585 --> 01:51:04.423
Because it doesn't matter who you are.

2944
01:51:04.423 --> 01:51:07.420
There's somebody, or something you have to forgive.

2945
01:51:07.420 --> 01:51:08.720
Yeah, everybody.

2946
01:51:08.720 --> 01:51:10.780
And it's easier to do that than hold on.

2947
01:51:10.780 --> 01:51:11.613
Right.

2948
01:51:11.613 --> 01:51:13.770
I wish people would do it more, honestly.

2949
01:51:13.770 --> 01:51:16.490
But, we dilute ourselves into thinking the easier path

2950
01:51:16.490 --> 01:51:17.640
is to hold onto it.

2951
01:51:17.640 --> 01:51:20.300
Like, there's the power of that, right?

2952
01:51:20.300 --> 01:51:23.800
Well, the ego is complete.

2953
01:51:23.800 --> 01:51:26.610
I think with the human body, like in the human mind.

2954
01:51:26.610 --> 01:51:29.540
Like we...

2955
01:51:29.540 --> 01:51:30.850
Again, back to patterns, right?

2956
01:51:30.850 --> 01:51:32.617
You see these patterns with people where it's like,

2957
01:51:32.617 --> 01:51:34.820
